0
00:00:01,367 --> 00:00:03,737
Tyra: PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"--

1
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:06,673
YAYA STRUGGLED
WITH THE JUDGES' FEEDBACK.

2
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:08,675
Nigel: YOU DON'T WANT
TO ALWAYS LOOK DANCER,

3
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:09,610
DANCER, DANCER,
DANCER, DANCER.

4
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:11,645
Yaya: BUT THAT IS
100% ME.

5
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,148
Tyra: RUMORS OF CASSIE'S
EATING DISORDER

6
00:00:15,148 --> 00:00:16,149
RIPPLED
THROUGH THE HOUSE.

7
00:00:16,717 --> 00:00:18,151
Cassie: BUT I DON'T WANNA
TALK ABOUT IT ANYMORE.

8
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:19,119
AND I DON'T WANT ANYONE ELSE
TALKING ABOUT IT.

9
00:00:20,053 --> 00:00:21,788
Tyra: CONTINUED CRITICISM
BROKE KELLE DOWN.

10
00:00:22,055 --> 00:00:23,557
Kelle: (sobs)

11
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:25,926
Tyra: BUT AT THE ELIMINATION
KELLE ADVANCED,

12
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:27,794
AND IT WAS JENNIPHER
WHO WAS SENT HOME.

13
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:29,630
ONLY NINE GIRLS REMAIN.

14
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:31,732
WHO WILL BE
ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

15
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,638
♪♪♪

16
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:15,375
Kelle: DADDY,

17
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:16,276
Man: Yeah?

18
00:01:16,276 --> 00:01:18,278
Kelle: I DON'T HAVE INTENSITY
IN MY EYES.

19
00:01:19,046 --> 00:01:21,682
I KEEP TRYING DIFFERENT THINGS
AND THINKING DIFFERENT THINGS.

20
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:24,451
AND I-I DON'T KNOW.

21
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:26,186
YESTERDAY
DURING ELIMINATION

22
00:01:26,186 --> 00:01:29,556
I HAD ANOTHER
NOT-SO-FLATTERING PHOTO.

23
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:30,691
Tyra: KELLE,

24
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:32,893
YOUR PICTURES HAVE BEEN,
LITERALLY,

25
00:01:33,126 --> 00:01:34,995
SOME OF THE WORST
IN THE BUNCH.

26
00:01:35,495 --> 00:01:36,863
Kelle: I DON'T KNOW WHAT
WHAT TO DO.

27
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:38,498
AND IT'S LIKE,
NO MATTER HOW HARD I TRY,

28
00:01:38,498 --> 00:01:39,433
I STILL
DON'T GET IT.

29
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:41,134
I JUST NEED HELP.

30
00:01:43,971 --> 00:01:44,638
Tyra: THANKS,
JENNIPHER.

31
00:01:45,372 --> 00:01:46,940
Cassie: JENN
WAS ELIMINATED.

32
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,309
OUT OF ALL THE GIRLS HERE,
WE HAD TALKED THE MOST.

33
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:51,612
I DON'T PARTICULARLY
GET ALONG

34
00:01:51,612 --> 00:01:53,213
WITH THE REST OF THE GIRLS
IN THE HOUSE.

35
00:01:53,547 --> 00:01:55,048
I'M A LONER
AND I'M USED TO IT.

36
00:01:55,048 --> 00:01:56,650
SO I'LL SIT ON MY BED
BY MYSELF,

37
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:57,384
AND I'LL BE FINE.

38
00:01:58,685 --> 00:01:59,620
Amanda: TRASH, TRASH,
TRASH,

39
00:02:00,153 --> 00:02:02,022
TRASH, TRASH, TRASH.

40
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:03,523
LOOK
AT THE TRASH.

41
00:02:04,491 --> 00:02:07,928
IT'S LIKE LIVING WITH
EIGHT OTHER BEAUTIFUL PIGS.

42
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:10,263
TRASH IN THERE
WITHOUT A TRASH BAG,

43
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,065
LEAVING FOOD
ON THE COUNTER,

44
00:02:12,065 --> 00:02:12,799
COME ON.

45
00:02:13,266 --> 00:02:15,002
THIS MORNING PEOPLE
WERE JUST PILING TRASH

46
00:02:15,002 --> 00:02:17,204
AROUND
THE GARBAGE CAN.

47
00:02:17,204 --> 00:02:19,172
Eva: AND WE KNOW
WHO THE PEOPLE ARE.

48
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:20,841
Amanda: BLAH, BLAH, BLAH,
BLAH... (blows raspberry)

49
00:02:21,274 --> 00:02:23,377
RIGHT NOW CASSIE IS PRETTY MUCH
THE SLOPPIEST ONE

50
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:27,180
WITH DIET COKES AND SUCH
STREWN ABOUT THE HOUSE.

51
00:02:27,581 --> 00:02:29,216
SHE'S A SLOPPY SLUT.

52
00:02:34,287 --> 00:02:34,921
Tyra: WAKE UP!

53
00:02:35,522 --> 00:02:37,290
Norelle: I LOVE THAT
TYRA BANKS CAME INTO OUR ROOM

54
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:38,659
AND JUMPED ON OUR BEDS
TO WAKE US UP.

55
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:40,560
LIKE, IT MAKES ME HAPPY,
'CAUSE SHE'S LIKE A REAL PERSON.

56
00:02:41,862 --> 00:02:43,196
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY,
SO TODAY

57
00:02:43,697 --> 00:02:45,732
I'M GONNA BE TALKING
ABOUT THE MODELING INDUSTRY

58
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:51,238
IN TERMS OF EATING, BODY IMAGE,
AND THE PRESSURES

59
00:02:51,238 --> 00:02:53,840
TO HAVE TO FIT INTO
A CERTAIN MOLD.

60
00:02:54,441 --> 00:02:55,242
I HAVE A FRIEND
OF MINE,

61
00:02:55,909 --> 00:02:57,077
HER NAME
IS KATE DILLON.

62
00:02:57,544 --> 00:03:00,347
KATE AND I USED TO MODEL
IN LOS ANGELES AND IN PARIS.

63
00:03:01,048 --> 00:03:02,349
AND SHE'S ONE OF THE TOP
PLUS-SIZED MODELS

64
00:03:02,349 --> 00:03:03,116
IN THE INDUSTRY.

65
00:03:04,985 --> 00:03:06,386
SO THIS IS
KATE DILLON.

66
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:06,787
Women: HEY!

67
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:14,361
Kate: I HAVE BEEN A MODEL
SINCE I WAS, GOSH, 17 YEARS OLD.

68
00:03:14,928 --> 00:03:17,030
AND I WAS THE FIRST PLUS-SIZED
MODEL EVER TO BE IN "VOGUE."

69
00:03:17,564 --> 00:03:19,299
Toccara: I THINK I STARED
AT KATE LIKE THE WHOLE TIME,

70
00:03:19,299 --> 00:03:21,401
LIKE, "WOW,
THAT'S GONNA BE ME."

71
00:03:21,401 --> 00:03:23,770
LIKE, I'M GONNA BE THE FIRST
BLACK PLUS-SIZED GIRL.

72
00:03:24,071 --> 00:03:25,706
Kate: I STARTED OUT
AS A SKINNY MODEL.

73
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:29,576
IN ORDER TO BE A "SKINNY" MODEL,
UM, YOU HAVE TO BE "SKINNY."

74
00:03:30,143 --> 00:03:31,878
AND FOR ME,
IT WAS REALLY, REALLY DIFFICULT.

75
00:03:32,345 --> 00:03:33,547
I ACTUALLY HAD
AN EATING DISORDER.

76
00:03:34,114 --> 00:03:35,348
I'D GO DAYS
WITHOUT EATING

77
00:03:35,348 --> 00:03:36,917
OR JUST MAYBE EATING,
YOU KNOW, AN APPLE

78
00:03:36,917 --> 00:03:37,651
OR SOMETHING
LIKE THAT.

79
00:03:38,485 --> 00:03:40,687
AND I COULDN'T STAY
IN THE BUSINESS AS I WAS.

80
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:41,855
I WAS UNHEALTHY.

81
00:03:42,289 --> 00:03:43,356
I WAS
MISERABLE.

82
00:03:44,024 --> 00:03:45,158
AND I ENDED UP QUITTING
THE BUSINESS.

83
00:03:45,459 --> 00:03:48,829
I GAINED, LIKE, 50 POUNDS
AND ENDED UP RETURNING,

84
00:03:48,995 --> 00:03:50,197
BUT AS
A PLUS-SIZED MODEL.

85
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:52,966
THIS MIGHT NOT BE
THE RIGHT CAREER FOR ANY OF YOU.

86
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,469
IF IT'S NOT THE RIGHT CAREER
FOR YOU,

87
00:03:55,469 --> 00:03:58,071
DON'T TRY TO MANIPULATE YOURSELF
AT ANY COST TO FIT INTO IT.

88
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:00,073
Tyra: IN A WAY
YOU GUYS ARE ATHLETES,

89
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:02,242
BECAUSE YOU HAVE TO WORK
ON YOUR BODY.

90
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:05,245
YOU HAVE TO STAY IN SHAPE,
AND YOUR CAREERS ARE TEMPORARY.

91
00:04:05,445 --> 00:04:08,448
SO WE'RE GONNA TALK TODAY
ABOUT HOW TO DO THIS HEALTHILY.

92
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:12,085
AND WE HAVE A WOMAN HERE
THAT IS GOING TO TALK TO YOU

93
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:13,286
ABOUT THAT
EVEN FURTHER.

94
00:04:13,987 --> 00:04:14,888
Woman: HEY!

95
00:04:15,288 --> 00:04:15,989
Tyra: COME AND SIT
RIGHT HERE.

96
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,358
Joy: FOR OVER 15 YEARS
I'VE BEEN WORKING WITH MODELS,

97
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:20,427
HELPING THEM TO MANAGE
THEIR WEIGHT.

98
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:25,132
IT'S ALL ABOUT BALANCING,
MODERATION AND CONSISTENCY.

99
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,568
Nicole: YEAH,
I DO, TOO.

100
00:04:28,568 --> 00:04:30,537
Joy: NOBODY NEEDS
TO BE AFRAID OF CARBOHYDRATE.

101
00:04:30,537 --> 00:04:33,373
CONTRARY TO WHAT THE REST OF THE
WORLD IS PREACHING RIGHT NOW,

102
00:04:33,907 --> 00:04:35,909
THESE ARE THE FOODS
THAT YOU NEED TO MODERATE,

103
00:04:36,143 --> 00:04:37,644
BUT NOT ELIMINATE.

104
00:04:38,044 --> 00:04:39,446
Tyra: I WANNA KNOW
IF ANYBODY WANTS TO DO

105
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:41,014
LIKE A ONE-ON-ONE
WITH THE THREE OF US.

106
00:04:42,182 --> 00:04:43,617
Cassie: WELL, I WANNA DO
A ONE-ON-ONE WITH YOU SOMETIME.

107
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:45,485
Tyra: SO IF EVERYONE ELSE CAN GO
INTO THE BEDROOMS FOR NOW.

108
00:04:47,921 --> 00:04:49,356
Cassie: YOU KNOW,
IF I WANNA BE A MODEL,

109
00:04:49,356 --> 00:04:51,291
I FEEL LIKE
I SHOULD BE SKINNY.

110
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:53,894
I WON'T SAY THAT I HAVE
A DISORDER,

111
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:57,030
BUT I WORRY ABOUT
WHAT I EAT 24/7.

112
00:04:58,031 --> 00:05:00,534
Joy: DO YOU EVER FEEL
THAT IT GETS OUT OF CONTROL

113
00:05:00,534 --> 00:05:02,435
AND THEN YOU DO A WHOLE
GUILT HEAD TRIP ON YOURSELF?

114
00:05:02,435 --> 00:05:04,137
Cassie: MM-HMM,
I HAVE HAD SEVERAL TIMES

115
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,472
WHERE I'VE THROWN UP
IN THE PAST.

116
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,575
BUT I NEVER CONSIDERED MYSELF
BULIMIC,

117
00:05:08,575 --> 00:05:10,844
BECAUSE I DIDN'T
THROW UP AFTER EVERY MEAL,

118
00:05:11,044 --> 00:05:14,181
AND I WOULD JUST DO IT AT NIGHT,
IF I THOUGHT I ATE TOO MUCH,

119
00:05:14,181 --> 00:05:15,816
AND I SHOULDN'T GO TO BED
WITH IT IN MY STOMACH.

120
00:05:16,483 --> 00:05:18,418
Joy: I GET NERVOUS WHEN
I HEAR THAT YOU'VE THROWN UP.

121
00:05:18,618 --> 00:05:20,387
DID YOU EVER TALK TO ANYBODY
ABOUT THAT?

122
00:05:20,387 --> 00:05:21,354
Cassie: MNH-MNH.

123
00:05:21,588 --> 00:05:24,457
Joy: MAYBE WE SHOULD EXPLORE
HAVING YOU TALK TO SOMEBODY,

124
00:05:24,457 --> 00:05:26,793
ONLY BECAUSE IT COULD REALLY
SPIRAL OUT OF CONTROL.

125
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:29,462
Tyra: ESPECIALLY
IN THIS ENVIRONMENT

126
00:05:30,263 --> 00:05:32,732
WITH THE PRESSURE
AND THE CRITIQUE.

127
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,202
Cassie: I DON'T FEEL LIKE
I CAN TALK TO SOMEONE

128
00:05:35,202 --> 00:05:36,736
AND THEY WILL KNOW
HOW I FEEL.

129
00:05:37,137 --> 00:05:39,506
YOU CAN TELL ME I SHOULDN'T
DO THAT ALL YOU WANT,

130
00:05:39,506 --> 00:05:41,508
BUT IF I FEEL LIKE I'M STILL
I'M STILL GONNA DO IT,

131
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:43,009
I'M NEVER
GONNA BE HELPED.

132
00:05:47,047 --> 00:05:48,215
Tyra: I WISH
SHE WOULD'VE...

133
00:05:49,249 --> 00:05:50,951
Kate: (whispers) PEOPLE WITH
EATING DISORDERS ARE HARD-CORE.

134
00:05:52,052 --> 00:05:53,720
Cassie: C.J.

135
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:54,487
C.J.: What's up?

136
00:05:55,488 --> 00:05:57,591
Cassie: I THINK THEY WANT ME
TO GO TO A COUNSELOR.

137
00:05:58,291 --> 00:05:58,892
C.J.: Why?

138
00:05:59,926 --> 00:06:00,794
Cassie:
FOR YOU KNOW WHAT.

139
00:06:01,294 --> 00:06:01,962
C.J.: They know?

140
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:02,896
Cassie: MM-HMM.

141
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:03,830
C.J.: How?

142
00:06:04,598 --> 00:06:05,098
Cassie:
I HAD TO TELL.

143
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:08,235
IF I'M FEELING THAT I'M HAPPY,
AND I'M DOING FINE,

144
00:06:08,235 --> 00:06:10,070
AND THIS IS MAKING ME HAPPY
BY DOING THIS,

145
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:11,404
THEN THAT'S ALL THAT MATTERS
TO ME.

146
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:25,619
Cassie: GIRLS,
THERE'S FOOD OUT THERE.

147
00:06:26,353 --> 00:06:27,587
IT'S JUST, LIKE,
FRUIT AND SALAD.

148
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,055
IT'S NOT LIKE A BUNCH
OF MEALS.

149
00:06:29,656 --> 00:06:30,523
Ann: I SMELL CAKE.

150
00:06:31,191 --> 00:06:31,958
Cassie: IT'S BROWNIES.

151
00:06:32,192 --> 00:06:34,394
Ann: CASSIE HAD MADE
BROWNIES.

152
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,029
YOU KNOW,
LOW CARB BROWNIES.

153
00:06:36,029 --> 00:06:37,364
THEY CAN ONLY
BE CASSIE'S

154
00:06:37,364 --> 00:06:38,732
BECAUSE WHO WOULD EAT
LOW CARB BROWNIES?

155
00:06:39,132 --> 00:06:41,067
Cassie: WHICH ARE
$6 A BAG,

156
00:06:41,201 --> 00:06:43,303
WHICH IS VERY EXPENSIVE
FOR A LITTLE THING OF BROWNIES.

157
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,438
Ann: AND THEY WERE SITTING
ON THE COUNTER

158
00:06:45,438 --> 00:06:48,375
WITH ALL OF THE STUFF OUT
THAT SHE USED TO MAKE THEM.

159
00:06:48,508 --> 00:06:49,676
Eva: UGH.

160
00:06:49,676 --> 00:06:50,710
SO IS YOUR OIL FINISHED?

161
00:06:51,311 --> 00:06:53,046
Ann: I WILL NOT COOK
IN A KITCHEN THAT'S DIRTY.

162
00:06:53,046 --> 00:06:54,381
LIKE,
THAT IS DISGUSTING.

163
00:06:54,614 --> 00:06:55,615
Eva: THIS PLACE
IS SO FRUSTRATING.

164
00:06:56,516 --> 00:06:57,117
Ann: IT'S DISGUSTING.

165
00:06:57,984 --> 00:06:59,052
LIKE, WHY IS THIS JUST
LYING HERE?

166
00:06:59,452 --> 00:07:00,420
Eva: UH, YEAH.

167
00:07:01,121 --> 00:07:01,988
Ann: WE SHOULD DRAW
IN IT.

168
00:07:02,322 --> 00:07:03,890
PUT,
"CASSIE, CLEAN YOUR DISHES."

169
00:07:04,557 --> 00:07:05,292
IS THAT RUDE?

170
00:07:05,492 --> 00:07:06,192
Eva: NO,
IT DOESN'T RUIN IT.

171
00:07:07,227 --> 00:07:08,261
Ann: CAN WE JUST
DRAW ON IT?

172
00:07:09,462 --> 00:07:10,196
A LITTLE ART CORNER.

173
00:07:11,631 --> 00:07:13,199
I WROTE WITH A KNIFE
IN HER BROWNIES.

174
00:07:14,901 --> 00:07:15,568
GO!

175
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:18,204
I'M LIKE, "EVA, YOU CAN BE
THE PATROL PERSON."

176
00:07:18,405 --> 00:07:19,706
BECAUSE WE HAD TO MAKE SURE
NO ONE WAS COMING.

177
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:24,477
EVA,
I CAN'T FIT "DISHES".

178
00:07:32,419 --> 00:07:33,119
Ann: COME LOOK.

179
00:07:34,421 --> 00:07:35,021
"CLEAN YOUR ..."

180
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,024
Eva: YES. YES.

181
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:39,993
Ann: I SHOULD'VE WROTE,
"EAT SOME CARBS."

182
00:07:40,527 --> 00:07:41,494
Eva: (laughs)

183
00:07:44,064 --> 00:07:45,098
Ann: I DO HAVE
A SENSE OF HUMOR.

184
00:07:45,265 --> 00:07:46,733
I THOUGHT MAYBE CASSIE
HAD ONE, TOO.

185
00:07:50,904 --> 00:07:52,472
Cassie: IT'S SO MIND-BOGGLING
TO ME

186
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,507
BECAUSE WHO WRITES
IN SOMEONE'S FOOD?

187
00:07:55,175 --> 00:07:55,742
WHO WROTE THAT?

188
00:07:56,409 --> 00:07:56,876
Eva: I DON'T KNOW.

189
00:07:57,577 --> 00:08:00,447
Yaya: SOMEONE HAD
THE AUDACITY TO MUTILATE

190
00:08:00,447 --> 00:08:02,082
HER PRECIOUS
BROWNIES.

191
00:08:02,382 --> 00:08:03,917
Toccara: YOU REALLY PISSED
ABOUT THEM BROWNIES.

192
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:06,453
Cassie: I AM, BECAUSE WHO
TOUCHES PEOPLE'S FOOD LIKE THAT?

193
00:08:06,453 --> 00:08:07,587
IT'S LIKE ME
STICKING MY HANDS

194
00:08:07,587 --> 00:08:09,189
ALL IN YOUR CHICKEN BREAST
OR SOMETHING.

195
00:08:09,189 --> 00:08:10,390
Ann: (whispers)
SHUT THAT.

196
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:11,391
Man: What?

197
00:08:11,391 --> 00:08:12,392
Ann: (whispers)
SHUT THE THING.

198
00:08:12,392 --> 00:08:13,560
HOLD ON, HOLD ON,
HOLD ON,

199
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,594
I'M TRYING
TO BE SNEAKY.

200
00:08:14,594 --> 00:08:16,029
Cassie: HEY,
AMANDA.

201
00:08:16,029 --> 00:08:17,097
Kelle: HI, THERE.

202
00:08:17,097 --> 00:08:17,998
Cassie: DID YOU WRITE
IN MY BROWNIES?

203
00:08:18,431 --> 00:08:19,099
Amanda: UNH-UNH.

204
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:20,100
Cassie: DO YOU KNOW
WHO DID?

205
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:20,967
Amanda: UNH-UNH.

206
00:08:20,967 --> 00:08:22,035
Cassie: OKAY,
JUST CHECKING.

207
00:08:22,035 --> 00:08:23,370
I QUESTIONED EVERYONE
IN THE HOUSE.

208
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:25,138
I JUST SAID,
"DID YOU WRITE IN MY BROWNIES?"

209
00:08:25,438 --> 00:08:26,973
Eva: I WOULD TELL YOU
IF I DID, BUT I DIDN'T.

210
00:08:27,774 --> 00:08:28,641
Cassie: OKAY,
THAT'S FINE.

211
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:29,242
I JUST--

212
00:08:29,376 --> 00:08:30,377
Toccara: WHO DID IT?

213
00:08:30,377 --> 00:08:30,977
Eva: NOT I.

214
00:08:31,644 --> 00:08:33,113
Cassie: EVA WAS LIKE,
"IT WASN'T ME,"

215
00:08:33,113 --> 00:08:35,682
BUT SHE WAS KINDA HINTING THAT
SHE KNEW IT WAS SOMEONE ELSE.

216
00:08:35,682 --> 00:08:39,152
AND WHO ELSE IS UNDER EVA'S BUTT
THE WHOLE TIME, EXCEPT ANN?

217
00:08:39,152 --> 00:08:40,486
Cassie: DID YOU WRITE
IN MY CAKE?

218
00:08:40,486 --> 00:08:41,421
Ann: NO.

219
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:42,688
Cassie: EVA SAID, "NO."

220
00:08:42,889 --> 00:08:44,691
YOU SAY "NO"
AND AMANDA SAID "NO," SO...

221
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:45,358
Ann: NOPE.

222
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:46,726
Cassie: OKAY.

223
00:08:46,726 --> 00:08:47,460
Ann: NO ONE WILL FESS UP
TO THAT.

224
00:08:47,794 --> 00:08:48,328
Yaya: IT WAS ONE
OF THOSE GIRLS.

225
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:49,362
Cassie: DUH.

226
00:08:49,462 --> 00:08:50,363
Ann: SHE'S
SO PISSED.

227
00:08:51,598 --> 00:08:52,632
Eva: SHE'S MAD,

228
00:08:53,299 --> 00:08:54,901
AND I DON'T CARE.

229
00:08:56,803 --> 00:08:58,405
Yaya: I'M WEARING THIS SHIRT
FOR YOU.

230
00:08:59,739 --> 00:09:02,008
RESPEITO--
IN PORTUGUESE

231
00:09:02,008 --> 00:09:05,645
CAN YOU SAY, "RESPECT"?
LIKE, "FALTA DO RESPEITO."

232
00:09:05,645 --> 00:09:07,247
IN THIS HOUSE
THERE'S NO RESPECT.

233
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,785
Amanda: NO ONE WOULD ADMIT
TO THE "INCIDENT."

234
00:09:11,785 --> 00:09:13,787
THE "BROWNIEGATE '04."

235
00:09:13,787 --> 00:09:16,890
Eva: WOW,
WHAT HAPPENED?

236
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:17,524
I COULD NOT
HELP LAUGHING.

237
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:21,928
Norelle:
IT WASN'T ME.

238
00:09:21,928 --> 00:09:23,496
Yaya: (laughs)

239
00:09:23,496 --> 00:09:23,945
Amanda: WE'RE LIKE,
"NOTHING."

240
00:09:23,945 --> 00:09:24,964
Cassie: SOMEONE NEEDS
TO TELL ME

241
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:27,700
WHO STUCK THEIR DAMN FINGERS
IN MY BROWNIES,

242
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,135
AND THEN THEY NEED
TO BUY ME SOME MORE BROWNIES.

243
00:09:29,135 --> 00:09:31,471
Toccara: SO IF NICOLE
DIDN'T DO IT,

244
00:09:31,538 --> 00:09:34,007
AND AMANDA DIDN'T DO IT,

245
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,276
AND KELLE
DIDN'T DO IT,

246
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:39,245
AND TOCCARA DIDN'T STEAL
THE COOKIES FROM THE COOKIE JAR,

247
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:42,315
AND YAYA DIDN'T STEAL THE
COOKIES FROM THE COOKIE JAR...

248
00:09:42,315 --> 00:09:44,284
♪ AND NORELLE DIDN'T STEAL THE
COOKIES FROM THE COOKIE JAR ♪♪

249
00:09:44,284 --> 00:09:45,452
Amanda: YEP, YEP.

250
00:09:45,452 --> 00:09:46,886
Toccara: ♪ AND EVA DIDN'T
STEAL-- ♪

251
00:09:49,322 --> 00:09:51,224
Amanda: MMM!

252
00:09:51,224 --> 00:09:52,225
Toccara: I'LL SEE Y'ALL
AT DINNER.

253
00:09:52,225 --> 00:09:54,527
Kelle: OH, YIKES.

254
00:09:54,527 --> 00:09:57,297
IT'S GONNA BE
SOME DRAMA.

255
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,571
Toccara: SO WE GET
TO THE DINNER,

256
00:10:04,571 --> 00:10:06,106
AND EVERYTHING IS KINDA,
LIKE, FINE.

257
00:10:06,106 --> 00:10:08,608
AND THEN ANN LOOKS OVER
AT YAYA,

258
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:11,845
AND SHE SAYS,
"WHAT DOES YOUR SHIRT MEAN?"

259
00:10:11,845 --> 00:10:12,879
Ann: YAYA,
WHAT DOES THAT--

260
00:10:12,879 --> 00:10:14,380
Yaya: IT'S RESPEITO.

261
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:15,915
IN PORTUGUESE,
IT MEANS "RESPECT."

262
00:10:16,416 --> 00:10:18,184
THERE'S A BIG LACK OF IT
IN THE HOUSE,

263
00:10:18,184 --> 00:10:19,719
SO I FELT THE NEED
TO WEAR IT TODAY.

264
00:10:19,719 --> 00:10:22,155
CASSIE'S BROWNIES
WERE FINGERED.

265
00:10:22,155 --> 00:10:23,456
I JUST THINK
IT MEANS THAT

266
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:24,724
THERE'S IMMATURITY IN RESPECT
IN THE HOUSE.

267
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:25,859
AND THAT WAS EXEMPT--

268
00:10:25,859 --> 00:10:26,893
Ann: WHY IS IT
IMMATURE?

269
00:10:26,893 --> 00:10:27,894
Yaya: WHY IS IT IMMATURE?

270
00:10:27,894 --> 00:10:29,195
Cassie: WHO WRITES
IN FOOD?

271
00:10:29,195 --> 00:10:30,563
WHO WRITES IN SOMEONE'S
BROWNIES?

272
00:10:30,563 --> 00:10:31,498
Ann: I WAS GONNA SAY
SOMETHING TO YOU ANYWAYS.

273
00:10:31,498 --> 00:10:32,732
I DID THAT TODAY
TO BE FUNNY.

274
00:10:32,732 --> 00:10:34,534
IT WASN'T TO BE--

275
00:10:34,534 --> 00:10:37,370
I DIDN'T DO IT TO HURT YOU
OR 'CAUSE I DON'T LIKE YOU.

276
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:39,172
OKAY, THAT'S FINE,

277
00:10:39,172 --> 00:10:40,607
IT WAS A JOKE,
I'M SORRY.

278
00:10:40,607 --> 00:10:41,708
I WAS TRYING TO BE FUNNY,
I THOUGHT YOU COULD--

279
00:10:41,708 --> 00:10:43,443
I THOUGHT YOU WOULD THINK
IT WAS FUNNY.

280
00:10:43,443 --> 00:10:44,878
Cassie: IT'S NOT FUNNY.

281
00:10:44,878 --> 00:10:46,446
Yaya: DO YOU HAVE A RELATIONSHIP
WITH CASSIE WHERE YOU THOUGHT

282
00:10:46,446 --> 00:10:47,714
THAT SHE HONESTLY
WOULD THINK IT WAS FUNNY?

283
00:10:47,714 --> 00:10:49,782
MAYBE IF YOU DID IT TO EVA,
YOU'D BE LIKE, "HA HA HA,"

284
00:10:49,782 --> 00:10:51,284
BUT THAT'S
NOT THE CASE.

285
00:10:51,284 --> 00:10:52,519
Ann: OKAY, I GUESS I LOOK
AT IT AS IF, LIKE,

286
00:10:52,519 --> 00:10:53,820
IF ONE OF YOU GUYS
DID THAT TO ME, I'D LAUGH.

287
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:56,156
Yaya: SOME PEOPLE THINK IT'S
FUNNY TO KILL PEOPLE.

288
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:57,624
THAT DOESN'T
MAKE IT FUNNY.

289
00:10:57,624 --> 00:10:59,759
Ann: OKAY, WELL, I'M SORRY
THAT YOU'RE SO MATURE

290
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:01,828
AND THAT YOU HAVE
NO SENSE OF HUMOR.

291
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,296
Cassie: I MEAN, WE DON'T HAVE
TO BE HOSTILE TO EACH OTHER,

292
00:11:03,296 --> 00:11:05,365
BUT DON'T TOUCH MY STUFF
'CAUSE IT'S NOT FUNNY TO ME.

293
00:11:05,365 --> 00:11:07,600
Ann: OKAY, WELL, WHEN YOU
WERE MAKING YOURSELF THROW UP

294
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,169
AND YOU DIDN'T WANT ANYONE
TO TALK ABOUT IT, YOU SAID THAT,

295
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:10,503
AND WE STOPPED TALKING
ABOUT IT.

296
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:11,871
Cassie: THAT'S FINE.

297
00:11:11,871 --> 00:11:13,473
Ann: SO STOP TALKING ABOUT
ME, BECAUSE I DON'T LIKE IT.

298
00:11:13,473 --> 00:11:14,874
Cassie: I'M GONNA TALK ABOUT
YOU, I'LL TELL YOU THAT NOW.

299
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:16,509
Ann: WELL, THEN I'M GONNA
TALK ABOUT HOW YOU'RE BULIMIC.

300
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:17,644
Cassie: THAT'S GREAT.

301
00:11:17,644 --> 00:11:18,545
Ann: I'LL TELL
TYRA TOMORROW.

302
00:11:18,545 --> 00:11:19,546
Cassie: SHE KNOWS,
ACTUALLY.

303
00:11:19,546 --> 00:11:20,244
WE TALKED
ABOUT IT TODAY.

304
00:11:20,244 --> 00:11:20,580
Ann: GOOD.

305
00:11:20,847 --> 00:11:21,648
Eva: LET'S TRY THIS.

306
00:11:21,648 --> 00:11:23,516
HOW ABOUT EVERYONE WASH
THEIR OWN DISHES?

307
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:24,617
Ann: CLEAN YOUR DISHES.

308
00:11:24,617 --> 00:11:26,953
DON'T BE A PIG--
THAT'S DISGUSTING.

309
00:11:26,953 --> 00:11:28,221
WHO WANTS TO LIVE WITH YOUR
DISHES IN THE SINK FOR A WEEK?

310
00:11:28,221 --> 00:11:29,622
Cassie: WHO WANTS TO LIVE
WITH YOU, ANN?

311
00:11:29,622 --> 00:11:32,592
OKAY, WELL
DON'T TOUCH MY...

312
00:11:32,592 --> 00:11:34,794
I DON'T NEED YOU TO TELL ME
TO WASH MY...

313
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:37,063
AND I DON'T NEED YOU TO PUT
A KNIFE IN MY BROWNIES

314
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:38,898
AND WRITE,
"CLEAN YOUR..."

315
00:11:38,898 --> 00:11:40,066
DON'T EVER
TOUCH MY STUFF.

316
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:50,510
Cassie: I DON'T NEED YOU
TO PUT A KNIFE IN MY BROWNIES

317
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:52,045
AND WRITE,
"CLEAN YOUR..."

318
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:55,081
DON'T EVER
TOUCH MY STUFF.

319
00:11:55,081 --> 00:11:56,649
Ann: CASSIE WILL NOT
DO HER DISHES.

320
00:11:57,617 --> 00:11:58,885
SO I WROTE WITH A KNIFE
IN HER BROWNIES.

321
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:01,120
IT WAS SUPPOSED TO BE, LIKE,
A JOKE.

322
00:12:01,321 --> 00:12:02,422
DID I RUIN IT?
DID I PISS ON IT?

323
00:12:02,689 --> 00:12:04,224
Cassie: IF I STUCK
MY FINGER IN YOUR CAKE

324
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:05,024
AND WENT LIKE THIS--

325
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:06,359
Ann: DID I USE
A FINGER?

326
00:12:06,359 --> 00:12:07,627
I USED A KNIFE,
HONEY.

327
00:12:07,627 --> 00:12:09,362
Yaya: THERE ARE OBVIOUSLY
MANY DIFFERENT LEVELS

328
00:12:09,362 --> 00:12:10,964
OF MATURITY AND EXPERIENCE
IN THIS HOUSE.

329
00:12:10,964 --> 00:12:12,966
WHETHER IT COMES TO WHAT KIND
OF SENSE OF HUMOR WE HAVE,

330
00:12:12,966 --> 00:12:14,834
OR HOW OFTEN WE WANNA
WASH OUR DISHES,

331
00:12:14,834 --> 00:12:18,371
WE ARE NOT THE SAME KINDS
OF PEOPLE, BUT RESPECT--

332
00:12:18,371 --> 00:12:19,806
RESPEITO IS THE ISSUE.

333
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,674
MOVING ON,
GROWING UP.

334
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,544
Cassie: I DON'T LIKE A LOT
OF DRAMA COMING FROM GIRLS,

335
00:12:24,544 --> 00:12:27,080
BUT WITH ANN,
THAT'S NOT AVOIDABLE HERE.

336
00:12:36,656 --> 00:12:38,291
Cassie:
I DON'T KNOW WHY

337
00:12:38,291 --> 00:12:40,093
THEY THINK THAT I'M THE ONLY ONE
THAT DOESN'T CLEAN MY DISHES,

338
00:12:40,393 --> 00:12:42,695
BECAUSE THERE'S A PILE
OF DISHES IN THE SINK RIGHT NOW,

339
00:12:42,695 --> 00:12:44,163
AND NONE OF THEM
ARE MINE.

340
00:12:44,731 --> 00:12:45,932
Ann: TYRA MAIL!

341
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:48,434
Nicole: "DO YOU HAVE WHAT
IT TAKES TO RISE TO THE TOP?

342
00:12:48,735 --> 00:12:50,670
"BE READY TO PROVE IT
AT 10:00."

343
00:12:51,204 --> 00:12:51,971
Women: YAY!

344
00:12:52,705 --> 00:12:55,341
♪♪♪

345
00:12:59,479 --> 00:13:01,814
Toccara: I STEP OUT
THE ELEVATOR, AND I'M LIKE,

346
00:13:02,215 --> 00:13:03,983
"AAH! THIS IS SO GREAT!

347
00:13:04,517 --> 00:13:05,451
I AM SO EXCITED!"

348
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:08,855
WE GOT THE ROPE COURSE,
THE WALLS, THE TIRES.

349
00:13:08,855 --> 00:13:10,790
OH, MY GOD!

350
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:12,125
Eva: EVERYBODY'S
JUMPING UP AND DOWN.

351
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:14,460
"YAY! YAY!"

352
00:13:15,595 --> 00:13:16,629
OKAY,
SO WHY ARE WE EXCITED?

353
00:13:17,096 --> 00:13:18,631
THIS IS
AN OBSTACLE COURSE.

354
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:21,668
Captain: GOOD MORNING,

355
00:13:21,668 --> 00:13:22,669
LADIES, I'M CAPTAIN
LEIF WADE--

356
00:13:23,036 --> 00:13:24,537
FORMER CAPTAIN
UNITED STATES MARINE CORPS.

357
00:13:25,371 --> 00:13:26,572
YOU ARE
NO LONGER CIVILIANS.

358
00:13:27,573 --> 00:13:29,676
YOU'RE RECRUITS
TO PURE POWER BOOT CAMP.

359
00:13:30,043 --> 00:13:31,144
Eva: BLAH, BLAH, BLAH,

360
00:13:31,144 --> 00:13:32,979
(imitates Captain)
TODAY IS ABOUT TENACITY,

361
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:35,515
STRENGTH, LOYALTY.

362
00:13:35,515 --> 00:13:37,850
Captain: WHEN YOU COME ACROSS
REJECTION IN THE MODELING WORLD,

363
00:13:37,850 --> 00:13:39,052
YOU CANNOT QUIT.

364
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:41,854
JUST LIKE I WILL NOT LET YOU
QUIT HERE TODAY.

365
00:13:42,455 --> 00:13:44,290
IT'S GONNA BE ONE OF THE HARDEST
WORKOUTS YOU'VE EVER DONE.

366
00:13:44,724 --> 00:13:46,859
("Reveille" playing)

367
00:13:46,859 --> 00:13:48,127
Yaya: I DON'T LIKE
PUTTING ON FATIGUES

368
00:13:48,528 --> 00:13:50,730
AND ACTING LIKE I'M GOING
THROUGH THE JUNGLE

369
00:13:50,730 --> 00:13:51,864
KILLING PEOPLE,
YOU KNOW?

370
00:13:51,864 --> 00:13:53,166
SO I WAS JUST NOT EXCITED
AT ALL.

371
00:13:53,533 --> 00:13:54,867
Ann: I WAS PUMPED AS HELL.

372
00:13:54,867 --> 00:13:56,436
I WORK OUT,
I PLAY WATER POLO.

373
00:13:56,803 --> 00:13:59,672
ACTUAL PHYSICAL ACTIVITY--
I FEED OFF THAT.

374
00:14:00,907 --> 00:14:02,241
Captain: ALL RIGHT, LADIES,
FALL IN.

375
00:14:02,709 --> 00:14:04,477
WATCH YOURSELF,
BE SAFE OUT HERE,

376
00:14:04,477 --> 00:14:05,511
MAXIMUM EFFORT,

377
00:14:05,812 --> 00:14:07,814
THREE... TWO... ONE!

378
00:14:07,914 --> 00:14:08,681
GO!

379
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:10,083
GO!

380
00:14:10,717 --> 00:14:11,584
WATCH YOUR KNEES.
GOOD!

381
00:14:11,718 --> 00:14:12,518
OH, YOU ALL RIGHT?

382
00:14:12,952 --> 00:14:13,753
I GOT YOU.

383
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:14,483
WATCH YOUR KNEES.
GOOD.

384
00:14:14,487 --> 00:14:14,852
WHOA.

385
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:19,959
COME ON. KICK THAT!

386
00:14:19,959 --> 00:14:20,793
NICE!

387
00:14:20,993 --> 00:14:22,862
Ann: EVERYTHING I'VE EVER DONE
I'VE BEEN GOOD AT

388
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,864
OR ONE OF
THE BEST PEOPLE,

389
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:25,965
SPORTS--
WHATEVER.

390
00:14:26,099 --> 00:14:30,203
Yaya: I DO FEEL EXTREME
COMPETITIVE ENERGY FROM ANN.

391
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:32,171
SHE'S THE TOP ATHLETE,

392
00:14:32,171 --> 00:14:36,242
AND I'M MAYBE SEEN AS ANOTHER
PHYSICAL PERSON BECAUSE I DANCE.

393
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,212
Captain: PULL,
PULL, PULL.

394
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:40,279
COME ON,
CASSIE, GET UP.

395
00:14:40,279 --> 00:14:41,547
GET UP, CASSIE,
COME ON,

396
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:44,117
Yaya: CASSIE JUST DIDN'T
WANT TO PARTICIPATE,

397
00:14:44,117 --> 00:14:47,487
AND SO SHE WAS DOING THINGS
KIND OF MINIMALLY.

398
00:14:47,487 --> 00:14:48,521
Captain: CASSIE,
LET'S GO.

399
00:14:48,521 --> 00:14:49,989
COME ON. BE PROUD.

400
00:14:49,989 --> 00:14:51,124
WHAT ARE YOU PROUD
OF HERE TODAY?

401
00:14:51,124 --> 00:14:52,291
Cassie: (sighs)
NOTHING,

402
00:14:52,291 --> 00:14:53,860
BECAUSE IF I WANTED TO GET
IN THE MILITARY,

403
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:54,994
I WOULD'VE SIGNED UP
FOR THE MILITARY.

404
00:14:54,994 --> 00:14:56,295
Captain: YOU'RE NOT HERE
TO GET IN THE MILITARY.

405
00:14:56,295 --> 00:14:59,165
Eva: CASSIE IS THE BIGGEST PUNK
I HAVE EVER MET.

406
00:14:59,165 --> 00:15:00,466
Cassie: I DON'T WANT
TO DO THIS ANYMORE.

407
00:15:00,466 --> 00:15:01,467
Captain: FLIP OVER.

408
00:15:01,467 --> 00:15:02,969
START DOING
PUSH-UPS.

409
00:15:02,969 --> 00:15:06,873
Amanda: I WANTED THE SERGEANT
TO REALLY JUST DRILL HER

410
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:08,508
AND YELL AT HER, SAY,

411
00:15:08,508 --> 00:15:09,842
(imitates Captain)
"YOU SUCK, YOU MAGGOT!

412
00:15:09,842 --> 00:15:11,711
"GET UP! AAH!
SHUT UP!"

413
00:15:11,811 --> 00:15:12,979
Cassie:
THIS IS DUMB.

414
00:15:12,979 --> 00:15:14,080
THIS IS
REALLY CHEESY.

415
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:16,416
I REALLY DON'T WANNA BE HERE
RIGHT NOW.

416
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:17,917
I WANNA GO HOME.

417
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:18,985
I WANNA GO BACK TO OKLAHOMA
RIGHT NOW.

418
00:15:18,985 --> 00:15:19,986
Captain:
BALANCE, FOCUS.

419
00:15:19,986 --> 00:15:21,053
Nicole: OH, YEAH!

420
00:15:21,053 --> 00:15:23,456
Eva: I THINK THE POINT
WAS TO TEACH US

421
00:15:23,456 --> 00:15:25,792
TENACITY
AND ENDURANCE

422
00:15:25,992 --> 00:15:29,162
AND WHEN IT SEEMS EXTREMELY
HARD, DON'T GIVE UP.

423
00:15:29,162 --> 00:15:30,430
TOP MODEL!

424
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,531
Captain:
THERE YOU GO.

425
00:15:31,531 --> 00:15:32,899
ALL RIGHT, LADIES,
LISTEN UP.

426
00:15:33,032 --> 00:15:35,134
HEY, SOME OF YOU DID
AN AMAZING JOB OUT HERE TODAY,

427
00:15:35,134 --> 00:15:38,304
SOME DIDN'T DO SO WELL,
AND YOU WILL SEE ME AGAIN.

428
00:15:38,304 --> 00:15:40,072
Women: UH-OH.

429
00:15:40,072 --> 00:15:41,941
Toccara: WE LEAVE
THE BOOT CAMP.

430
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,042
Women: BYE!

431
00:15:43,042 --> 00:15:45,378
Toccara: WE DRIVE
TO ANOTHER LOCATION.

432
00:15:49,582 --> 00:15:51,050
Norelle: THERE'S
CAPTAIN WADE AGAIN.

433
00:15:51,451 --> 00:15:52,452
(imitates Captain)
HELLO, LADIES.

434
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:53,619
Captain:
HELLO, LADIES.

435
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,520
Women: HELLO, CAPTAIN.

436
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:56,122
Captain: DIDN'T THINK YOU'D
SEE ME SO SOON?

437
00:15:56,122 --> 00:15:56,989
Women: NO.

438
00:15:57,557 --> 00:15:58,558
Captain: YOUR CHALLENGE
TODAY

439
00:15:58,558 --> 00:15:59,959
IS A RACE TO THE TOP
OF THE STAIRS

440
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,861
IN THIS 14-STORY
HIGH-RISE.

441
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:04,163
Toccara: WE'RE LIKE...

442
00:16:05,698 --> 00:16:06,833
"ARE YOU KIDDING ME?"

443
00:16:07,099 --> 00:16:08,000
Captain: THE WINNER
WILL BE BASED

444
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,469
ON THE BEST
INDIVIDUAL TIME.

445
00:16:09,836 --> 00:16:12,672
WHOEVER WINS THIS
WILL BE GREATLY REWARDED.

446
00:16:13,339 --> 00:16:14,774
SO BATTLE IT OUT
AMONGST YOURSELVES,

447
00:16:14,774 --> 00:16:16,342
AND WE'LL SEE WHO HAS
WHAT IT TAKES

448
00:16:16,342 --> 00:16:17,310
TO MAKE IT
TO THE TOP.

449
00:16:19,879 --> 00:16:21,647
Cassie: STAIRS SUCK,
AND I HATE 'EM.

450
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:23,182
Yaya: I JUST LOOKED AT IT
LIKE, "OH, I CAN DO THIS."

451
00:16:23,549 --> 00:16:24,784
Ann: IT WAS REALLY JUST
ME AND YAYA WHO WERE LIKE,

452
00:16:24,784 --> 00:16:26,719
"LET'S, LIKE, DO THIS."

453
00:16:26,719 --> 00:16:28,721
LIKE, YOU KNOW,
I WAS EXCITED.

454
00:16:28,721 --> 00:16:31,491
Eva: SO WE GO UP
THE FLIGHT OF STAIRS ONE BY ONE.

455
00:16:31,491 --> 00:16:32,425
I'M FIRST.

456
00:16:33,359 --> 00:16:33,993
Man: GO!

457
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:34,961
Ann: GO, EVA!

458
00:16:36,729 --> 00:16:37,230
Man: GO!

459
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:37,897
Ann: GO, KELLE!

460
00:16:38,364 --> 00:16:40,099
Man: GO!
Ann: GO, CASSIE!

461
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:41,701
Man: GO!

462
00:16:42,034 --> 00:16:42,735
GO!

463
00:16:49,876 --> 00:16:51,878
Eva: I'M RUNNING, I'M RUNNING.
I'M RUNNING.

464
00:16:52,378 --> 00:16:53,379
I DON'T HAVE
NO MORE BREATH.

465
00:16:59,819 --> 00:17:01,020
Kelle: UM,
IT'S REALLY HARD,

466
00:17:01,053 --> 00:17:03,523
BECAUSE I'M NOT AN ATHLETE
IN THE SLIGHTEST BIT.

467
00:17:04,423 --> 00:17:05,191
Toccara:
I DID PRETTY GOOD.

468
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:08,361
I GOT TO THE SEVENTH FLOOR
BEFORE I WAS LIKE, "UGH."

469
00:17:09,929 --> 00:17:12,131
Yaya: EVEN WHEN I WANTED
TO STOP ON THE STAIRWELL,

470
00:17:12,131 --> 00:17:13,098
I DIDN'T.

471
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:14,599
AND I MIGHT'VE
SLOWED DOWN,

472
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:16,402
BUT I DIDN'T
JUST STOP.

473
00:17:18,069 --> 00:17:19,438
Ann: I DON'T FAIL
AT THINGS.

474
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:21,040
I DON'T NOT
FINISH THINGS.

475
00:17:21,574 --> 00:17:22,842
Cassie: I WAS
WHEEZING LIKE...

476
00:17:22,842 --> 00:17:24,076
(wheezes)

477
00:17:24,076 --> 00:17:25,478
I COULD BARELY BREATHE,
YOU KNOW,

478
00:17:25,478 --> 00:17:26,811
'CAUSE I DIDN'T
WANT TO FINISH LAST.

479
00:17:27,946 --> 00:17:28,948
Eva: (panting)

480
00:17:28,948 --> 00:17:29,916
Captain: 1.33.

481
00:17:31,017 --> 00:17:33,085
TOP MODEL NEEDS TO LOOK GOOD
ON A MOMENT'S NOTICE.

482
00:17:33,085 --> 00:17:34,387
YOU NOW HAVE
A PHOTO SHOOT.

483
00:17:35,454 --> 00:17:36,622
Eva: (retches)

484
00:17:37,089 --> 00:17:38,090
YOU HAVE TO BE
KIDDING ME.

485
00:17:38,925 --> 00:17:40,359
I CAN'T
EVEN BREATHE.
(retches)

486
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:42,762
(retches)

487
00:17:43,696 --> 00:17:44,830
SO I JUST DECIDED,

488
00:17:44,997 --> 00:17:46,966
"HELL, I'M GONNA SMILE
IN THESE PICTURES."

489
00:17:55,007 --> 00:17:55,508
Captain: GOOD.

490
00:17:56,342 --> 00:17:57,443
YOU HAVE
A PHOTO SHOOT.

491
00:17:57,677 --> 00:17:58,511
Kelle:
A PHOTO SHOOT NOW?

492
00:17:58,811 --> 00:17:59,512
Eva: YEAH.

493
00:18:04,784 --> 00:18:07,820
Yaya: THE REAL CHALLENGE IS
IF I'M ON A PHOTO SHOOT

494
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:10,056
AFTER NOT HAVING SLEPT,
AFTER NOT HAVING EATEN--

495
00:18:10,489 --> 00:18:11,123
WHOO!

496
00:18:11,657 --> 00:18:12,391
IT'S NOT GOOD!

497
00:18:13,426 --> 00:18:15,895
IT'S IMPORTANT TO BE ABLE
TO JUST HAVE THAT ENDURANCE.

498
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:17,797
Captain: GOOD.

499
00:18:18,397 --> 00:18:19,298
YOU NOW HAVE
A PHOTO SHOOT.

500
00:18:19,999 --> 00:18:20,700
Ann: YOU KNOW,

501
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,935
THE MOST IMPORTANT THING TO ME
IS TO HAVE A GOOD PICTURE.

502
00:18:23,502 --> 00:18:25,571
AND I'VE ONLY HAD ONE
WHERE THEY ACTUALLY WERE LIKE,

503
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:27,106
"THAT'S BEAUTIFUL.
WE LIKE IT."

504
00:18:27,573 --> 00:18:28,608
Captain: YOU NOW HAVE
A PHOTO SHOOT.

505
00:18:29,375 --> 00:18:29,875
Amanda: OKAY.

506
00:18:38,918 --> 00:18:39,919
Captain: YOU GOT
A PHOTO SHOOT.

507
00:18:40,019 --> 00:18:40,853
Toccara: NO,
I DON'T.

508
00:18:41,087 --> 00:18:42,421
Captain: OH, YEAH,
COME ON.
Toccara: NO,
I DON'T.

509
00:18:43,689 --> 00:18:44,724
OH, I'M JUST POSING?

510
00:18:44,724 --> 00:18:45,157
Ché: YEAH.

511
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:48,194
Toccara: I THINK
THAT PHOTO SHOOT SUCKED.

512
00:18:53,566 --> 00:18:54,600
Captain: ON YOUR FEET,
LADIES!

513
00:18:56,102 --> 00:18:57,670
NONE OF YOU QUIT,
ALL RIGHT?

514
00:18:57,670 --> 00:18:59,639
WHICH IS THE MOST IMPORTANT
THING HERE.

515
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:01,474
THE TIMES
WERE VERY CLOSE.

516
00:19:01,474 --> 00:19:03,843
IN 9th PLACE
IS KELLE--2.34.

517
00:19:04,543 --> 00:19:06,379
Kelle: I WASN'T REALLY
EXPECTING TO WIN

518
00:19:06,379 --> 00:19:08,581
'CAUSE THERE ARE SO MANY GIRLS
FAR MORE ATHLETIC THAN ME.

519
00:19:08,881 --> 00:19:10,316
Captain: EIGHTH--
NORELLE.

520
00:19:10,449 --> 00:19:11,884
SEVENTH--
TOCCARA.

521
00:19:11,884 --> 00:19:12,685
Ann: GOOD FOR TOCCARA,

522
00:19:13,085 --> 00:19:14,553
BUT, LIKE, HOW DOES NORELLE
AND KELLE FEEL

523
00:19:14,553 --> 00:19:15,955
THAT THEY JUST
LOST TO, YOU KNOW,

524
00:19:15,955 --> 00:19:18,958
A GIRL THAT WEIGHS
50 MORE POUNDS THAN THEM?

525
00:19:18,958 --> 00:19:19,992
Captain: SIXTH--AMANDA.

526
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,661
FIFTH IS CASSIE.

527
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:23,029
Cassie: I WAS JUST HAPPY
I GOT TO THE TOP

528
00:19:23,029 --> 00:19:24,363
AND DIDN'T FINISH LAST.

529
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,132
Captain: FOURTH
IS NICOLE.

530
00:19:26,132 --> 00:19:27,800
THIRD IS EVA.

531
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:29,669
Toccara: IT WAS BETWEEN
YAYA AND ANN.

532
00:19:31,037 --> 00:19:35,408
Captain: TODAY'S WINNER...
YAYA.

533
00:19:35,408 --> 00:19:36,575
Yaya: WHOO!

534
00:19:36,942 --> 00:19:37,777
Captain: 1.10.

535
00:19:38,711 --> 00:19:39,278
Yaya: YEAH!

536
00:19:39,979 --> 00:19:42,715
Captain: NOW, YAYA,
YOU GET TO PICK ONE PERSON.

537
00:19:43,949 --> 00:19:45,851
Yaya: I PICK TOCCARA!

538
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:46,952
Toccara: YEAH!

539
00:19:46,952 --> 00:19:47,953
Captain: ALL RIGHT.

540
00:19:48,421 --> 00:19:49,789
Yaya: TOCCARA WAS ONE
OF THE PEOPLE THAT REALLY

541
00:19:49,789 --> 00:19:53,325
EXEMPLIFIED NOT GIVING UP
AND SURPASSING EXPECTATIONS.

542
00:19:53,926 --> 00:19:56,095
Captain: YOU TWO BEAUTIFUL
LADIES ARE GONNA ENJOY

543
00:19:56,095 --> 00:19:59,131
A WONDERFUL, BEAUTIFUL EVENING
HERE AT CLAY SPA,

544
00:19:59,432 --> 00:20:00,466
UP HERE
ON THIS ROOF DECK.

545
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:01,867
Toccara: OOH.

546
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:02,668
Yaya: YAY!

547
00:20:02,802 --> 00:20:04,437
Captain: THE REST OF YOU LADIES
ARE NOT SO LUCKY.

548
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:07,606
YOU HAVE
TO WALK HOME.

549
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:12,278
Norelle: AFTER THAT
BRUTAL DAY WE HAD?

550
00:20:12,645 --> 00:20:14,547
Ann: DOES ANYONE EVEN KNOW
WHICH WAY WE'RE SUPPOSED TO GO?

551
00:20:14,814 --> 00:20:15,848
Eva: RIGHT OR LEFT?

552
00:20:15,848 --> 00:20:16,849
Kelle: RIGHT.

553
00:20:16,849 --> 00:20:18,317
Cassie: MAKE A RIGHT.

554
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:24,390
Cassie: SO YAYA AND TOCCARA
GOT TO STAY

555
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:25,491
AND DO
THEIR LITTLE FACIALS.

556
00:20:26,492 --> 00:20:28,861
Eva: THE PERSON THAT NEEDED
THE FACIAL, GOT THE FACIAL.

557
00:20:33,499 --> 00:20:34,767
Amanda:
♪ ADVENTURES ♪

558
00:20:34,934 --> 00:20:36,202
♪ WITH A BLIND TOOL ♪♪

559
00:20:43,008 --> 00:20:45,177
AND 20 BLOCKS IN NEW YORK
EQUALS ONE MILE.

560
00:20:45,845 --> 00:20:46,378
Amanda: REALLY?

561
00:20:46,412 --> 00:20:46,777
Kelle: YEAH.

562
00:20:49,615 --> 00:20:50,382
Yaya: I KNOW.

563
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:52,084
Toccara: JUST
TO BE OUTSIDE.

564
00:20:52,585 --> 00:20:54,820
Yaya: EVERY PANEL
I'VE BEEN CRITICIZED

565
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:58,924
FOR LETTING MY DANCERISH-NESS
SHINE THROUGH.

566
00:20:59,391 --> 00:21:00,459
Tyra: WHEN I LOOKED
AT THE PICTURE,

567
00:21:00,459 --> 00:21:01,861
I DID NOT SEE
A MODEL.

568
00:21:02,027 --> 00:21:03,229
IT WAS TOO DANCER.

569
00:21:03,629 --> 00:21:04,830
Nigel: IT WAS ALMOST
TOO DRAMATIC.

570
00:21:05,397 --> 00:21:06,732
Yaya: WHAT I'M STRUGGLING WITH
RIGHT NOW IS

571
00:21:06,732 --> 00:21:09,502
HOW TO SET ASIDE
SOMETHING

572
00:21:09,502 --> 00:21:13,706
THAT IS SO MUCH
A PART OF ME, YOU KNOW?

573
00:21:13,706 --> 00:21:14,507
Toccara: RIGHT.

574
00:21:14,507 --> 00:21:16,342
Yaya: YOU KNOW, LIKE,
THE DEFINITION OF "YAYA"--

575
00:21:16,342 --> 00:21:17,610
DANCE IS UP THERE.

576
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:25,918
Cassie:
I THINK I HAD

577
00:21:25,918 --> 00:21:27,787
THE HOLLYWOOD IMAGE
OF NEW YORK CITY IN MY HEAD.

578
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,889
AND WHEN I CAME HERE,
I WAS SO DISAPPOINTED BY IT.

579
00:21:29,889 --> 00:21:33,392
IT'S HARD TO COME HERE
AND SEE JUST THIS BIG PLACE

580
00:21:33,392 --> 00:21:35,127
WHERE IT'S REALLY DIRTY,
AND IT'S REAL EXPENSIVE.

581
00:21:35,861 --> 00:21:36,428
Kelle: YOU GUYS,

582
00:21:36,428 --> 00:21:37,830
WE'RE GONNA MAKE A LEFT
AT THIS CORNER.

583
00:21:38,631 --> 00:21:40,099
Eva: KELLE
WAS OUR TOUR GUIDE.

584
00:21:40,399 --> 00:21:42,201
WELL, THIS IS ALL CALLED
GREENWICH VILLAGE.

585
00:21:42,668 --> 00:21:44,770
FOLLOW ME, LADIES.
FOLLOW THE HAND.

586
00:21:44,904 --> 00:21:47,606
FINALLY,
SOMETHING I CAN DO.

587
00:21:47,606 --> 00:21:48,674
OH, MY GOD.

588
00:21:53,345 --> 00:21:54,346
(knock on door)

589
00:21:54,346 --> 00:21:54,747
Ann: HELLO.

590
00:21:55,381 --> 00:21:56,649
Cassie: HAPPINESS TO ME

591
00:21:56,649 --> 00:21:58,317
IS JUST THAT FEELING
THAT CAN'T BE DESCRIBED,

592
00:21:58,784 --> 00:22:00,486
AND IT'S NOT HERE
RIGHT NOW.

593
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,755
I DON'T WANNA LIVE
IN NEW YORK CITY

594
00:22:02,755 --> 00:22:04,623
IF I DON'T HAVE THAT FEELING
IN MY HEART, YOU KNOW?

595
00:22:04,623 --> 00:22:06,225
RIGHT NOW
I DON'T HAVE IT.

596
00:22:06,592 --> 00:22:08,594
BEING IN THIS COMPETITION,
I DON'T HAVE IT.

597
00:22:08,594 --> 00:22:11,363
NEW YORK IS NOT AS GLAMOROUS
AS I PICTURED IT TO BE,

598
00:22:11,363 --> 00:22:12,998
AND THAT'S WHY I THINK
I'M SO DISAPPOINTED.

599
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:14,300
'CAUSE IT WAS ALWAYS,
LIKE,

600
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:16,502
MY DREAM CITY THAT I NEVER
THOUGHT I WOULD GET TO GO TO.

601
00:22:16,502 --> 00:22:17,736
AND NOW I'M HERE,
AND I HATE IT.

602
00:22:18,571 --> 00:22:20,306
I FEEL LIKE ALL MY SPIRIT
IS GONE HERE.

603
00:22:21,507 --> 00:22:22,641
C.J.: Just be
a trooper.

604
00:22:22,641 --> 00:22:23,709
Cassie: I'LL TRY MY BEST.

605
00:22:24,543 --> 00:22:25,611
C.J.: Try my best?

606
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:27,847
Cassie: WILL YOU BE MAD
IF I COME HOME EARLY?

607
00:22:38,323 --> 00:22:39,925
Kelle: YOU GUYS,
TYRA MAIL!

608
00:22:40,258 --> 00:22:42,761
"LIGHTS, CAMERA, ACTION.

609
00:22:42,761 --> 00:22:46,498
"TOMORROW GET A JUMP START TO
YOUR DAY AND BE READY AT 7:30."

610
00:22:46,631 --> 00:22:47,532
Toccara: OKAY.

611
00:22:58,710 --> 00:22:59,678
Jay: GOOD MORNING.

612
00:23:00,445 --> 00:23:02,147
SO I KNOW YOU GUYS
ARE ALREADY THINKING,

613
00:23:02,147 --> 00:23:03,582
"WHAT THE HECK?"

614
00:23:04,316 --> 00:23:07,519
NOW SOME OF YOU STILL HAVE
ISSUES POSING ON THE GROUND,

615
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:09,254
BUT TODAY IT'S
EVEN MORE CHALLENGING,

616
00:23:09,254 --> 00:23:11,857
BECAUSE YOU NEED TO LEARN
HOW TO POSE

617
00:23:12,124 --> 00:23:13,358
WHILE IN FLIGHT
IN THE AIR.

618
00:23:14,292 --> 00:23:15,894
Ann: HONESTLY,
MY HEART STOPPED.

619
00:23:16,027 --> 00:23:17,696
I'M DEATHLY AFRAID
OF AIRPLANES.

620
00:23:17,696 --> 00:23:19,464
Jay: SO, OF COURSE,
TO DO THIS SHOOT RIGHT,

621
00:23:19,464 --> 00:23:21,366
I HAD TO GET A PHOTOGRAPHER
THAT'S SHOT TYRA,

622
00:23:21,366 --> 00:23:22,767
AND HIS NAME
IS SASCHA PFLAEGING.

623
00:23:22,767 --> 00:23:25,770
Sascha: IT'S GONNA BE REALLY
DEMANDING PHYSICALLY TODAY.

624
00:23:26,104 --> 00:23:27,472
I HOPE YOU ALL HAVE
A LOT OF ENERGY.

625
00:23:28,006 --> 00:23:29,141
Jay: ALL RIGHT,
LET'S DO IT.

626
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:34,045
Amanda: WE WERE THINKING THAT
WE WERE GONNA, LIKE,

627
00:23:34,045 --> 00:23:35,614
BUNGEE JUMP
FROM AN AIRPLANE,

628
00:23:35,614 --> 00:23:37,182
LIKE OVER THE WATER,

629
00:23:37,182 --> 00:23:39,651
LAND ON A BOAT WITH, LIKE,
A THING OF YOGURT OR SOMETHING.

630
00:23:39,651 --> 00:23:40,919
WE HAD NO IDEA.

631
00:23:41,052 --> 00:23:42,521
Jay: HEY, DANILO,
MATHU,

632
00:23:42,521 --> 00:23:44,489
CAN I TAKE THOSE GIRLS FROM YOU
FOR JUST A SECOND?

633
00:23:44,789 --> 00:23:47,659
OKAY, THE SHOOT TODAY
IS FOR YJ STINGER.

634
00:23:47,659 --> 00:23:49,327
IT'S AN ENERGY DRINK.

635
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:52,130
SO THIS IS AN ACTION SHOT TODAY,
ALL RIGHT?

636
00:23:52,130 --> 00:23:53,465
WE HAVE
A BIG TRAMPOLINE.

637
00:23:53,732 --> 00:23:56,368
Amanda: THE TRAMPOLINE
OF DOOM!

638
00:23:56,368 --> 00:23:59,070
Jay: AND YOU HAVE TO LEARN
HOW TO BOUNCE, GIVING ME FACE,

639
00:23:59,070 --> 00:24:01,406
GIVING ME BODY
IN THE AIR, OKAY?

640
00:24:02,073 --> 00:24:03,675
Kelle: I GUESS I DON'T
DEAL WELL WITH, LIKE,

641
00:24:03,675 --> 00:24:05,043
"YEAH,
YOU'RE DOING GREAT,"

642
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:06,645
'CAUSE I'M NOT REALLY
DOING GREAT.

643
00:24:06,645 --> 00:24:08,346
SO TELL ME, LIKE,
"YOU'RE NOT DOING THIS RIGHT"

644
00:24:08,346 --> 00:24:10,115
AS OPPOSED TO, LIKE,
"YEAH, YOU'RE DOING GREAT"

645
00:24:10,115 --> 00:24:11,783
AND THEN EXPECTING ME
TO DO BETTER.

646
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:13,218
Jay: BUT, YOU KNOW,
AT THE SAME TIME, KELLE,

647
00:24:13,218 --> 00:24:14,786
I CAN'T BABY YOU
THROUGH EVERY FRAME.

648
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:16,388
I'M TIRED OF TALKING
ABOUT KELLE.

649
00:24:16,388 --> 00:24:17,522
I'M TIRED
OF TALKING TO KELLE.

650
00:24:17,522 --> 00:24:19,124
I'M TIRED
OF SEEING KELLE CRY.

651
00:24:19,424 --> 00:24:21,660
Kelle: ACCEPTED THE FACT THAT
I CAN'T TAKE A GOOD PICTURE,

652
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:23,295
BUT NOW I'M TRYING
TO WORK ON THAT,

653
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:24,529
AND I KEEP ON WITH IT.

654
00:24:24,529 --> 00:24:25,664
(sniffles)
WHATEVER.

655
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:27,299
I NEED HELP.

656
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:28,733
I'VE NEVER
DONE THIS BEFORE.

657
00:24:28,733 --> 00:24:31,036
IF I COULD TAKE PERFECT PHOTOS
AND I KNEW WHAT I WAS DOING,

658
00:24:31,036 --> 00:24:32,604
I'D BE IN AN AGENCY.

659
00:24:32,604 --> 00:24:34,406
Ann: SHE WASN'T SAYING,
"BABY ME ALONG."

660
00:24:34,406 --> 00:24:36,474
ALL SHE WAS SAYING WAS
IF SHE'S DOING BAD,

661
00:24:36,474 --> 00:24:38,076
DON'T TELL HER
SHE'S DOING GOOD.

662
00:24:38,243 --> 00:24:39,611
Sascha: ALL RIGHT,
LET'S GO.

663
00:24:39,611 --> 00:24:41,346
THREE. GOOD.

664
00:24:41,580 --> 00:24:42,414
THREE.

665
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:44,349
Jay: GOOD FACE.

666
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:46,151
Sascha: CASSIE--

667
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:47,752
SHE'S VERY COMFORTABLE
JUMPING UP AND DOWN.

668
00:24:47,752 --> 00:24:49,254
THERE WERE SOME
REALLY NICE MOVES

669
00:24:49,254 --> 00:24:51,122
AND SOME REALLY
BEAUTIFUL SHOTS,

670
00:24:51,423 --> 00:24:54,559
BUT CASSIE DIDN'T HAVE
A LOT OF VARIETY.

671
00:24:54,559 --> 00:24:55,160
Sascha: ONE...

672
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:56,494
TWO...

673
00:24:57,162 --> 00:24:57,528
THREE. NICE.

674
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:00,131
Jay: EVA WAS EXCITED,

675
00:25:00,131 --> 00:25:02,701
AND SHE REALLY
GAVE ME ENERGY.

676
00:25:02,701 --> 00:25:04,135
Sascha: SHE'S GOOD.

677
00:25:04,135 --> 00:25:04,803
SHE'S REALLY NICE.
SHE'S PRETTY.

678
00:25:05,303 --> 00:25:06,504
BUT IT'S JUST NOT
A LOT OF RANGE.

679
00:25:06,805 --> 00:25:07,672
Michelle: PERFECT.

680
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:10,075
Mathu: IT'S A GOOD THING.

681
00:25:10,408 --> 00:25:11,643
Michelle: AND WE ARE
IN AGGREEANCE?

682
00:25:11,643 --> 00:25:12,811
THIS IS HER OUTFIT,
ALL RIGHT?

683
00:25:13,645 --> 00:25:16,181
Sascha: ONE... TWO...

684
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:17,015
THREE...

685
00:25:17,449 --> 00:25:21,219
FOR BEING A LITTLE BIGGER GIRL,
TOCCARA WAS REALLY GOOD.

686
00:25:21,553 --> 00:25:22,587
THREE.

687
00:25:23,054 --> 00:25:24,322
Nicole: IT'S TRICKY
ON THE TRAMPOLINE.

688
00:25:24,322 --> 00:25:26,358
YOU HAD TO KEEP A LOT OF FACTORS
IN MIND--THE DRESS,

689
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:27,592
THE PRODUCT
YOU'RE SELLING,

690
00:25:27,592 --> 00:25:28,426
YOUR FACE.

691
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:32,697
Eva: DO DIFFERENT STUFF
WITH YOUR ARMS.

692
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:34,833
REMEMBER THAT YOU GOTTA
PRESENT THE CAN.

693
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:36,768
Sascha: NORELLE IS
A LITTLE BIT SCRAWNY

694
00:25:36,768 --> 00:25:38,069
AND A LITTLE BONY,

695
00:25:38,536 --> 00:25:41,239
BUT FOR HER THIS SITUATION
MADE IT EVEN MORE DIFFICULT

696
00:25:41,339 --> 00:25:44,175
TO FIND A VERY NICE,
GOOD-LOOKING, ELEGANT POSITION.

697
00:25:44,542 --> 00:25:45,610
Norelle: WHAT'S WRONG
WITH ME?

698
00:25:47,112 --> 00:25:47,912
Kelle: HI.
I'M KELLE.

699
00:25:48,246 --> 00:25:49,614
Sascha: HI KELLE,
NICE TO MEET YOU.

700
00:25:49,614 --> 00:25:51,349
Kelle: I HAD
A REALLY CUTE DRESS

701
00:25:51,349 --> 00:25:52,784
I WAS SO EXCITED
TO WEAR,

702
00:25:52,784 --> 00:25:54,452
THEN I START JUMPING,

703
00:25:54,452 --> 00:25:56,655
AND MY ENTIRE TOP
COMES OUT OF MY DRESS,

704
00:25:57,155 --> 00:25:58,790
Woman: JUST A SEC.

705
00:25:58,790 --> 00:26:01,126
Yaya: DON'T KEEP DOING IT,
PLEASE.

706
00:26:01,126 --> 00:26:02,594
Kelle: THIS IS
THE PROBLEM.

707
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:03,662
Yaya: LOOK. AAH!

708
00:26:04,663 --> 00:26:05,630
Kelle: AAH!

709
00:26:06,197 --> 00:26:07,065
Sascha: WARDROBE?

710
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:09,868
Kelle: AND SO MICHELLE HAD
TO TRY TO FIND ANOTHER DRESS.

711
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,369
Michelle: YOU'RE BOUNCING
AROUND IN THERE?

712
00:26:11,369 --> 00:26:12,103
NOTHING'S HAPPENING?

713
00:26:15,206 --> 00:26:16,074
Sascha: THREE...

714
00:26:16,608 --> 00:26:17,342
JUST KEEP
YOUR LEGS UP.

715
00:26:17,709 --> 00:26:18,643
STRAIGHT LOOKING
AT THE LIGHTS.

716
00:26:18,643 --> 00:26:19,444
JUST... YEAH.

717
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:22,447
AND LOOK
INTO THE LIGHT,

718
00:26:23,148 --> 00:26:24,316
JUST THROW YOUR NECK BACK
A LITTLE BIT.

719
00:26:24,783 --> 00:26:26,785
Jay: KELLE IS JUST
SO SELF-CONSCIOUS

720
00:26:26,785 --> 00:26:29,287
THAT SHE FLUNKS
AS A MODEL

721
00:26:29,287 --> 00:26:30,522
WHEN SHE GETS IN FRONT
OF THE CAMERA.

722
00:26:31,489 --> 00:26:34,392
Kelle: I DON'T REALLY HAVE
ANYTHING POSITIVE TO GO ON

723
00:26:34,392 --> 00:26:35,960
AS TO WHY I AM HERE.

724
00:26:36,194 --> 00:26:38,096
I MEAN,
IT'S REALLY HARD,

725
00:26:38,096 --> 00:26:40,398
ESPECIALLY WHEN YOU'RE LOOKING
IN THE MIRROR AND, YOU KNOW,

726
00:26:40,398 --> 00:26:41,666
YOU'RE BREAKING
YOUR FACE APART

727
00:26:41,666 --> 00:26:43,468
AND YOU JUST WONDER,

728
00:26:43,468 --> 00:26:45,370
"HOW CAN I EVER MAKE THIS LOOK
PRETTY ON FILM?"

729
00:26:46,037 --> 00:26:48,473
AND THEN YOU GET HERE,
AND YOU CAN'T.

730
00:26:48,740 --> 00:26:50,475
IT'S REALLY HARD.

731
00:26:52,210 --> 00:26:52,944
Michelle: LET ME SEE,
HONEY.

732
00:26:52,944 --> 00:26:53,411
TURN AROUND.

733
00:26:55,146 --> 00:26:56,181
YEAH, AND THEN
YOU'RE GONNA JUMP.

734
00:26:56,181 --> 00:26:57,182
LIKE,
HOLD IT AND JUMP.

735
00:26:57,182 --> 00:26:58,149
LET'S SEE.
I WANNA MAKE SURE.

736
00:26:58,149 --> 00:26:59,084
OOH!

737
00:26:59,084 --> 00:27:00,819
I KEEP FORGETTING
YOU GIRLS ARE SO TALL.

738
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:04,522
Ann: I HAVE TO PROVE
THAT I DESERVE TO BE HERE,

739
00:27:04,856 --> 00:27:06,725
BECAUSE I'VE ONLY HAD
ONE GOOD PICTURE

740
00:27:07,192 --> 00:27:08,893
OUT OF ALL THE SHOOTS
WE'VE DONE.

741
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:10,528
Sascha: ONE... TWO...

742
00:27:10,528 --> 00:27:11,096
THREE.

743
00:27:13,565 --> 00:27:16,034
ANN DIDN'T SEEM TO BE BOTHERED
BY HURTING HERSELF,

744
00:27:16,167 --> 00:27:17,736
SO SHE REALLY GAVE A LOT
INTO IT.

745
00:27:19,137 --> 00:27:20,672
THREE. GOOD.
BEAUTIFUL.

746
00:27:20,672 --> 00:27:21,740
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

747
00:27:21,740 --> 00:27:23,108
Ann: YEAH.

748
00:27:23,108 --> 00:27:23,942
Sascha: LESS IS MORE.

749
00:27:24,209 --> 00:27:25,076
Ann: LESS IS MORE.
OKAY.

750
00:27:26,010 --> 00:27:29,013
Jay: ANN WAS JUST
A BIG FLOP.

751
00:27:31,383 --> 00:27:32,584
LITERALLY,
SHE FLOPPED.

752
00:27:32,584 --> 00:27:33,752
SHE SCRAPED
HER CHIN.

753
00:27:33,752 --> 00:27:34,486
SHE SCRAPED
HER ELBOWS.

754
00:27:35,286 --> 00:27:36,287
SHE LOOKS
A MESS.

755
00:27:36,788 --> 00:27:37,655
Ann: I TRIED TO FLY,

756
00:27:38,390 --> 00:27:40,458
AND I DON'T KNOW
IF IT WORKED OR NOT.

757
00:27:40,592 --> 00:27:42,394
Jay: SHE'S GOT THAT FACE,
THAT...

758
00:27:43,595 --> 00:27:44,329
THAT'S ANN.

759
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:45,697
Ann: OW.
IS IT BLEEDING?

760
00:27:46,097 --> 00:27:46,698
Man: A LITTLE BIT.

761
00:27:47,465 --> 00:27:48,633
Danilo: SHAPE--

762
00:27:48,633 --> 00:27:50,535
PROBABLY WANT A LITTLE TIGHTER
RIGHT THERE.

763
00:27:51,102 --> 00:27:53,438
Yaya: ACCORDING TO
SOME OF THE PANELISTS,

764
00:27:53,438 --> 00:27:55,840
MY PHOTOS LOOK
LIKE A DANCER.

765
00:27:56,474 --> 00:27:58,610
AND SOME OF THEM I LIKED
THAT THE PANEL DIDN'T LIKE.

766
00:27:58,610 --> 00:27:59,411
Danilo: YEAH.

767
00:27:59,677 --> 00:28:01,179
Yaya: ON SOME OF THEM,

768
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:01,846
THE PANEL LIKED
AND I DIDN'T LIKE.

769
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:03,782
Danilo: GOD BLESS
THE PANEL.

770
00:28:05,483 --> 00:28:08,319
Yaya: ANY INSTINCTUAL POSES
THAT I WOULD DO

771
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:11,589
MIGHT HAVE TRACES
OF "DANCERATION" IN IT,

772
00:28:11,589 --> 00:28:13,391
SO I TRIED
TO STRIP THAT AWAY,

773
00:28:13,792 --> 00:28:17,162
AND I THINK IT ENDED UP MAKING
MY SHOOT A LITTLE BIT BORING.

774
00:28:17,495 --> 00:28:17,996
Sascha: THREE.

775
00:28:19,164 --> 00:28:20,465
Jay: YAYA TOOK HER ADVICE
FROM THE PANEL

776
00:28:20,465 --> 00:28:21,966
AND TOOK IT
TO THE EXTREME,

777
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:24,035
WHICH, IN THAT CASE,
ISN'T HELPING HER.

778
00:28:27,138 --> 00:28:28,640
Sascha: AMANDA
WAS BEAUTIFUL.

779
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:29,841
SHE HAD IT ALL.

780
00:28:30,175 --> 00:28:31,176
SHE SHOWED
A LOT OF VARIETY,

781
00:28:31,242 --> 00:28:32,377
AND SHE WORKED
WITH HER BODY.

782
00:28:33,044 --> 00:28:34,078
Eva: SHE'S KICKING ASS.

783
00:28:34,245 --> 00:28:35,180
Mathu: SHE IS KICKING
MAJOR ASS.

784
00:28:35,713 --> 00:28:36,548
Yaya: AMANDA,
GO HOME.

785
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:38,650
Eva: AMANDA WAS DOING
DANCER-LIKE POSES,

786
00:28:38,650 --> 00:28:40,418
AND YAYA WAS GETTING PISSY
OVER THERE.

787
00:28:41,286 --> 00:28:42,120
Yaya: OKAY.

788
00:28:42,587 --> 00:28:44,823
SO FUNNY.
THIS IS JUST FUNNY.

789
00:28:46,524 --> 00:28:47,525
THIS IS FUNNY.

790
00:28:47,725 --> 00:28:49,194
Eva: "IT'S NOT FAIR.

791
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:50,261
"THEY TOLD ME I CAN'T DO
DANCER POSES,

792
00:28:50,261 --> 00:28:51,429
"AND WATCH, THEY'LL LOVE
AMANDA'S POSES."

793
00:28:51,696 --> 00:28:52,964
Jay: COME HERE
FOR A SECOND, PLEASE.

794
00:28:54,065 --> 00:28:55,567
I JUST WANT YOU
TO UNDERSTAND,

795
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:57,335
LIKE, YOU SUPER
IMPRESSED ME.

796
00:28:57,335 --> 00:28:58,670
I DIDN'T SAY A WORD.

797
00:28:58,670 --> 00:29:00,505
IN MY OPINION,

798
00:29:00,505 --> 00:29:01,739
YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE
WHO GOT THIS TODAY,

799
00:29:02,106 --> 00:29:03,374
AND I HAVEN'T COMMENTED
ON ANYONE TODAY.

800
00:29:03,641 --> 00:29:04,542
Amanda: THANK YOU
SO MUCH.

801
00:29:04,709 --> 00:29:05,176
THAT MEANS A LOT.

802
00:29:05,844 --> 00:29:06,511
Yaya: I'M REALLY MAD

803
00:29:06,511 --> 00:29:08,446
THAT I DIDN'T DO
WHAT I WANTED TO--

804
00:29:08,446 --> 00:29:09,247
YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M SAYING?

805
00:29:09,481 --> 00:29:10,682
Eva: YAYA GOES,
"WELL,

806
00:29:10,682 --> 00:29:12,684
THEY TOLD ME I CAN'T DO
DANCER-LIKE POSES,"

807
00:29:12,684 --> 00:29:15,220
SO THERE'S ALWAYS AN EXCUSE
FOR EVERYTHING.

808
00:29:15,487 --> 00:29:17,956
CAN IT BE BECAUSE
YOU'RE NOT PERFECT?

809
00:29:18,323 --> 00:29:20,492
NO. MISS YAYA
DOESN'T THINK SO.

810
00:29:21,759 --> 00:29:23,528
Yaya: AFTERWARD,
I DID SOME COOL STUFF,

811
00:29:23,528 --> 00:29:25,129
AND JAY WAS LIKE, "WHY DIDN'T
YOU DO THAT UP THERE?"

812
00:29:25,330 --> 00:29:27,165
EVERY WEEK I GET
THE SAME COMMENT, LIKE,

813
00:29:27,165 --> 00:29:28,600
"THERE GOES
THAT DANCER THING."

814
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:30,468
Jay: YOU SHOULDN'T
TAKE EVERYTHING

815
00:29:30,468 --> 00:29:32,470
AS A HARD-AND-FAST RULE,
'CAUSE YOU KNOW WHAT?

816
00:29:32,470 --> 00:29:34,272
IN THIS WORLD, TEN PEOPLE ARE
GONNA SAY, "DON'T DO THIS.

817
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:35,573
"DON'T DO THIS.
DON'T DO THIS.

818
00:29:35,573 --> 00:29:37,108
"DON'T DO THIS."

819
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:38,576
YOU KNOW WHAT
YOU'RE GONNA END UP WITH?

820
00:29:38,576 --> 00:29:39,210
NOTHIN' TO DO.

821
00:29:39,511 --> 00:29:40,512
Yaya: HMM.

822
00:29:48,386 --> 00:29:49,487
Cassie: TYRA MAIL.

823
00:29:49,654 --> 00:29:50,722
Eva: TYRA MAIL!

824
00:29:50,722 --> 00:29:52,090
Cassie: "TOMORROW YOU MEET
WITH THE JUDGES.

825
00:29:52,090 --> 00:29:54,459
ONLY EIGHT OF YOU WILL
CONTINUE ON IN HOPES OF BECOMING

826
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:55,860
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

827
00:29:55,860 --> 00:29:57,128
ONE OF YOU
WILL BE ELIMINATED."

828
00:29:57,128 --> 00:29:58,897
Ann: IT'S GETTING DOWN
TO THE WIRE THAT THERE ARE

829
00:29:58,897 --> 00:30:00,899
ENOUGH PEOPLE THAT ARE DOING
CONSISTENTLY GOOD

830
00:30:00,899 --> 00:30:03,268
THAT YOU CAN'T AFFORD TO HAVE
A BAD WEEK HERE,

831
00:30:03,735 --> 00:30:05,170
SO I WILL BE NERVOUS.

832
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:15,413
Tyra: HELLO, EVERYBODY.

833
00:30:15,413 --> 00:30:16,347
Women: HELLO.

834
00:30:16,948 --> 00:30:19,517
Tyra: THIS WEEK,
YOU LEARNED ALL ABOUT FITNESS

835
00:30:19,517 --> 00:30:21,786
AND THE IMPORTANCE
OF BEING MOTIVATED

836
00:30:21,786 --> 00:30:23,121
AND WANTING IT.

837
00:30:23,488 --> 00:30:25,190
BUT NOW IT'S TIME
TO MAKE OUR SIXTH CUT

838
00:30:25,623 --> 00:30:27,492
TOWARDS DETERMINING
WHO WILL BECOME

839
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:28,893
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

840
00:30:28,893 --> 00:30:30,228
WE HAVE
SOME AMAZING PRIZES--

841
00:30:30,728 --> 00:30:34,732
A MODEL CONTRACT WITH THE TOP
INTERNATIONAL MODELING AGENCY

842
00:30:34,732 --> 00:30:35,934
FORD MODELS,

843
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:37,936
A SPREAD
IN "ELLE" MAGAZINE

844
00:30:37,936 --> 00:30:40,638
WITH WORLD-RENOWNED PHOTOGRAPHER
GILLES BENSIMONE,

845
00:30:41,105 --> 00:30:46,077
AND A $100,000 CONTRACT
WITH COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

846
00:30:46,077 --> 00:30:46,911
Janice: WOW.

847
00:30:47,412 --> 00:30:48,112
Tyra: AND OF COURSE,

848
00:30:48,112 --> 00:30:50,248
YOU KNOW,
WE HAVE SOME JUDGES.

849
00:30:50,548 --> 00:30:52,083
FIRST IS
MISS JANICE DICKINSON.

850
00:30:52,083 --> 00:30:54,452
JANICE IS THE VERY FIRST
SUPERMODEL

851
00:30:54,452 --> 00:30:56,254
EVER TO EXIST
ON THIS PLANET.

852
00:30:56,921 --> 00:31:00,091
WE ALSO HAVE NIGEL BARKER,
A NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER,

853
00:31:00,959 --> 00:31:03,895
NOLE MARIN, A PROMINENT
FASHION EDITOR AND STYLIST.

854
00:31:03,895 --> 00:31:05,029
Nolé: HOW ARE YOU,
LADIES?

855
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:06,030
MINI SAYS HI.

856
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:07,131
Women: HEY!

857
00:31:07,832 --> 00:31:10,368
Tyra: AND OUR GUEST JUDGE
FOR THIS WEEK IS KATE DILLON,

858
00:31:10,568 --> 00:31:13,004
WHO IS A FELLOW
TOP MODEL HERSELF.

859
00:31:13,004 --> 00:31:14,105
Kate: HI, YOU GUYS.

860
00:31:14,105 --> 00:31:14,672
YOU GUYS
LOOK AMAZING.

861
00:31:15,773 --> 00:31:19,477
Tyra: WHAT MAKES A TOP MODEL
IS HER ABILITY TO BE ON POINT

862
00:31:19,477 --> 00:31:22,046
NO MATTER HOW TIRED OR EXHAUSTED
SHE IS.

863
00:31:22,547 --> 00:31:24,782
SO WE HAD A PHOTOGRAPHER
STANDING BY TO TAKE YOUR PICTURE

864
00:31:24,782 --> 00:31:28,353
AFTER YOU RAN UP
14 FLIGHTS OF STAIRS.

865
00:31:28,486 --> 00:31:29,754
Woman: OH, NO!

866
00:31:30,588 --> 00:31:31,890
Tyra: THAT DAY
YOU WERE GETTING PHOTOGRAPHED

867
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,691
IS YOUR TEST TODAY.

868
00:31:33,925 --> 00:31:35,226
Women: OHH!

869
00:31:35,793 --> 00:31:37,529
Tyra: YOU WILL ALSO BE TESTED
ON YOUR PHOTO

870
00:31:37,529 --> 00:31:39,964
THAT YOU TOOK
ON A TRAMPOLINE FOR YJ STINGER.

871
00:31:39,964 --> 00:31:41,533
WE HAVE RANDOMLY
DRAWN NAMES,

872
00:31:41,833 --> 00:31:43,701
AND, NORELLE,
YOU'RE FIRST.

873
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:47,672
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY,
NORELLE,

874
00:31:47,805 --> 00:31:50,041
SO HERE IS YOUR EXHAUSTED
PHOTO SHOOT.

875
00:31:51,709 --> 00:31:52,610
Janice: WOW.

876
00:31:53,111 --> 00:31:54,579
SHE DOESN'T
LOOK EXHAUSTED.

877
00:31:54,579 --> 00:31:56,180
SHE LOOKS LIKE
SHE'S IN PAIN.

878
00:31:56,548 --> 00:31:57,849
Nolé: I ACTUALLY
LIKE IT.

879
00:31:57,849 --> 00:32:01,486
I THINK IT'S EXTREMELY MODERN,
KIND OF GRUNGY-LOOKING.

880
00:32:01,486 --> 00:32:02,787
Tyra: ALL RIGHT, NORELLE,
SO YOU HAD A PHOTO SHOOT

881
00:32:02,787 --> 00:32:04,322
WHERE YOU HAD TO JUMP
ON A TRAMPOLINE,

882
00:32:04,722 --> 00:32:06,324
AND LET'S SEE
HOW YOU DID.

883
00:32:06,958 --> 00:32:07,892
Janice: LOVELY.

884
00:32:08,459 --> 00:32:09,260
Nolé: OH, NORELLE,
AMAZING.

885
00:32:09,527 --> 00:32:10,094
Janice: VERY LOVELY.

886
00:32:10,094 --> 00:32:11,262
Kate: YOUR FACE LOOKS
VERY RELAXED,

887
00:32:11,262 --> 00:32:12,697
WHICH I THINK
IS VERY DIFFICULT

888
00:32:12,697 --> 00:32:14,532
WHEN YOU'RE TENSING
YOUR MUSCLES AND JUMPING.

889
00:32:14,699 --> 00:32:15,400
I'M VERY
IMPRESSED.

890
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:16,334
Norelle:
THANK YOU.

891
00:32:17,135 --> 00:32:17,501
Tyra: KELLE.

892
00:32:19,671 --> 00:32:21,139
Janice: IT'S REALLY BAD,
I'M SORRY.

893
00:32:21,639 --> 00:32:22,674
I CAN'T EVEN
LOOK AT IT.

894
00:32:23,041 --> 00:32:23,975
IT'S THAT BAD.

895
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:25,343
Nigel: LOOKING AT YOU,

896
00:32:25,677 --> 00:32:26,411
YOU'VE GOT
A GREAT BODY.

897
00:32:27,011 --> 00:32:29,147
IN THIS PICTURE HERE,
THOSE LEGS ACTUALLY LOOK BIG,

898
00:32:29,147 --> 00:32:30,815
YOUR STOMACH
LOOKS BIG.

899
00:32:30,815 --> 00:32:32,150
Janice: YOUR GUT'S
HANGING OUT, YOU KNOW...

900
00:32:32,150 --> 00:32:35,086
Tyra: "A" FOR EFFORT,
BUT "F" FOR THE END PRODUCT.

901
00:32:36,955 --> 00:32:37,755
Nigel:
TOO CONTRIVED.

902
00:32:38,189 --> 00:32:39,390
YOU'RE THINKING ABOUT IT
ALL TOO MUCH.

903
00:32:39,857 --> 00:32:41,259
Janice: WE'VE NEVER SEEN
EXPRESSION IN YOUR FACE.

904
00:32:41,259 --> 00:32:42,760
IT'S ALWAYS
THE SAME THING.

905
00:32:42,994 --> 00:32:44,062
Nolé: KELLE, WHAT DID YOU DO
BEFORE YOU CAME HERE?

906
00:32:44,195 --> 00:32:44,996
WHAT WAS
YOUR LIFE ABOUT?

907
00:32:45,697 --> 00:32:46,931
Kelle: UM, I ACTUALLY OWN
AN ART GALLERY.

908
00:32:47,098 --> 00:32:48,299
Janice: HAVE YOU HEARD
OF EXPRESSIONISM?

909
00:32:49,100 --> 00:32:49,634
HERE.

910
00:32:50,068 --> 00:32:50,568
Kelle: YEAH.

911
00:32:51,669 --> 00:32:53,104
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY,
UP NEXT WE HAVE NICOLE.

912
00:32:55,306 --> 00:32:58,843
Janice: YOU DON'T REALLY LOOK
LIKE A MODEL IN THIS PICTURE.

913
00:32:59,143 --> 00:33:00,912
Nolé: EVERY TIME
A CAMERA'S ON YOU,

914
00:33:00,912 --> 00:33:02,246
YOU SHOULD
ALWAYS TRY TO STRIKE A POSE,

915
00:33:02,246 --> 00:33:03,181
'CAUSE YOU NEVER KNOW.

916
00:33:03,181 --> 00:33:03,848
Tyra: YES.

917
00:33:03,848 --> 00:33:05,316
Nolé: I MEAN,
I'M WITH THIS GIRL A LOT,AND
SHE'S-- HELLO.

918
00:33:05,316 --> 00:33:06,417
Tyra: EVEN WHEN WE DO
SNAPSHOTS-- YEAH, I'M TIRED.

919
00:33:06,417 --> 00:33:08,553
I WAKE UP,
WHEN I SEE A CAMERA.

920
00:33:08,553 --> 00:33:09,721
Nolé: SHE SNAPS IT UP,
LIKE, AMAZING.

921
00:33:09,721 --> 00:33:11,556
Nigel: WHOA. OOH. GOOD.

922
00:33:11,556 --> 00:33:12,724
Janice: WOW.
THAT'S FIERCE.

923
00:33:12,724 --> 00:33:13,725
Nigel: WHOA!

924
00:33:13,725 --> 00:33:14,459
Nolé: FIERCE.

925
00:33:14,926 --> 00:33:16,327
Tyra: YOU KNOW WHAT
I LIKE ABOUT IT?

926
00:33:16,327 --> 00:33:17,362
THAT IT DOESN'T LOOK LIKE
SOME OF THE GIRLS.

927
00:33:17,362 --> 00:33:18,363
THEY HELD IT LIKE...

928
00:33:18,363 --> 00:33:20,732
(breathy voice)
"HEY! YJ STINGER."

929
00:33:20,732 --> 00:33:22,400
(normal voice) YOU KNOW,
AND THAT'S NOT FASHION.

930
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:23,701
THIS IS FASHION.

931
00:33:24,569 --> 00:33:26,137
UP NEXT
WE HAVE TOCCARA.

932
00:33:29,307 --> 00:33:30,174
LOOK AT THAT.

933
00:33:30,408 --> 00:33:31,776
THE INTENSITY
WITH NO HAIR AND MAKEUP.

934
00:33:31,776 --> 00:33:32,810
Nigel: YEAH.

935
00:33:33,344 --> 00:33:35,046
Tyra: SO YOU HAD
A PHOTO SHOOT ON A TRAMPOLINE.

936
00:33:36,481 --> 00:33:39,283
Nolé: YOU LOOK KINDA LIKE
A RAGING BULL--FLARING NOSTRILS.

937
00:33:39,283 --> 00:33:40,351
I DON'T KNOW
ABOUT THIS.

938
00:33:40,618 --> 00:33:42,720
Kate: YOU HAVE WHAT
A LOT OF PLUS-SIZED MODELS HAVE,

939
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:45,189
WHICH IS A SENSE OF FREEDOM
IN THEIR BODY,

940
00:33:45,323 --> 00:33:48,192
AND THAT KIND OF ENERGY
OBVIOUSLY REALLY SHOWS THROUGH.

941
00:33:48,192 --> 00:33:49,260
Tyra: CASSIE.

942
00:33:51,429 --> 00:33:53,931
Kate: I THINK THE POSES
ARE A LITTLE TOO MODEL-Y.

943
00:33:53,931 --> 00:33:55,033
A LITTLE TOO, LIKE...

944
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:56,668
Tyra: HERE'S
YOUR BEST SHOT.

945
00:33:56,668 --> 00:33:57,669
Janice: HELP ME.

946
00:33:57,835 --> 00:33:58,736
Nigel: (laughing)

947
00:33:58,736 --> 00:33:59,937
Tyra: I LIKE IT.

948
00:34:00,405 --> 00:34:01,839
Cassie: WHOA,
I LOOK SCARY.

949
00:34:01,839 --> 00:34:03,875
Janice: YOU LOOK LIKE
YOU BELONG IN A CORNFIELD,

950
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:06,210
LIKE SCARING CROWS AWAY.

951
00:34:06,210 --> 00:34:07,845
(imitates crow cawing)

952
00:34:09,179 --> 00:34:10,248
Tyra: THE PHOTOGRAPHER
SAID

953
00:34:10,248 --> 00:34:11,416
THAT "CASSIE LOOKS TIRED
AND WEAK

954
00:34:11,416 --> 00:34:13,384
AND NOT SURE
IF SHE REALLY WANTS TO BE HERE."

955
00:34:13,384 --> 00:34:14,619
Janice: WHAT'S UP
WITH THAT?

956
00:34:15,219 --> 00:34:16,219
Cassie: I DON'T KNOW.

957
00:34:16,353 --> 00:34:17,388
Tyra: EVA.

958
00:34:17,688 --> 00:34:18,822
WELL, HOW DID YOU FEEL?

959
00:34:18,822 --> 00:34:20,324
Eva: TIRED.
I GAGGED.

960
00:34:20,324 --> 00:34:21,592
I WAS ONE OF THE FEW GIRLS
THAT GAGGED.

961
00:34:21,592 --> 00:34:22,760
Nigel: THE FACT THAT YOU WERE
ABOUT TO BE SICK--

962
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:24,862
I MEAN, THIS IS
PRETTY PULLED TOGETHER.

963
00:34:25,797 --> 00:34:27,331
THAT'S BEAUTIFUL.

964
00:34:27,598 --> 00:34:28,866
Janice: YOU LOOK 5'11"
IN THIS PHOTOGRAPH.

965
00:34:28,866 --> 00:34:30,201
Kate: YOU DO LOOK 5'11".

966
00:34:30,201 --> 00:34:31,034
Janice:
MISS SHORTY GIRL.

967
00:34:31,235 --> 00:34:32,070
Tyra: CAN WE SEE
A CLOSEUP?

968
00:34:32,704 --> 00:34:34,539
Janice: YOU CAN'T SEE THE FLARED
NOSTRIL THINGIE ANYMORE.

969
00:34:34,539 --> 00:34:36,440
YOU JUST HAVE TO BRING
YOUR HEAD DOWN A LITTLE

970
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:38,242
AND KIND OF KEEP THE NOSE
TOGETHER.

971
00:34:39,277 --> 00:34:40,277
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY,
AMANDA,

972
00:34:40,277 --> 00:34:41,079
HERE ARE
YOUR THREE SHOTS.

973
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:42,847
Janice: NOT BAD.

974
00:34:42,847 --> 00:34:43,915
Kate: NOT BAD
AT ALL.

975
00:34:43,915 --> 00:34:44,282
Nolé: GORGEOUS,
ACTUALLY.

976
00:34:44,282 --> 00:34:44,982
Kate: NOT BAD AT ALL
Nolé: BEAUTIFUL.

977
00:34:45,149 --> 00:34:46,384
Nigel: ONE OF THE MOST
STARTLING THINGS ABOUT THIS

978
00:34:46,384 --> 00:34:48,886
IS NORMALLY WHAT MAKES YOUR
PICTURES GREAT ARE YOUR EYES,

979
00:34:48,886 --> 00:34:51,022
AND YOU REALLY CAN'T SEE THEM
IN ANY OF THE PICTURES,

980
00:34:51,022 --> 00:34:52,223
AND YOU STILL
LOOK GOOD.

981
00:34:53,357 --> 00:34:53,991
Janice: GORGEOUS.

982
00:34:55,592 --> 00:34:57,562
YOU'VE GOT A CLASSIC,
TIMELESS LOOK HERE.

983
00:34:57,829 --> 00:34:59,030
Tyra: THE PHOTOGRAPHER
COMMENTS WERE

984
00:34:59,030 --> 00:35:00,965
THAT YOU WERE
THE SUPERSTAR OF THE SHOOT.

985
00:35:03,401 --> 00:35:04,569
ALL RIGHTY,
UP NEXT WE HAVE YAYA.

986
00:35:05,737 --> 00:35:06,938
SO YOU WON THE RACE,

987
00:35:07,638 --> 00:35:08,473
AND HERE ARE
YOUR THREE PICTURES FROM IT.

988
00:35:09,907 --> 00:35:12,176
Nigel: IT'S VERY SPORTS PERSON
KIND OF PHOTOGRAPHS,
BUT THAT'S NICE.

989
00:35:12,176 --> 00:35:13,778
Tyra: THEY'RE NOT BAD.
Janice: BEAUTIFUL,
THAT'S AWESOME.

990
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:16,814
NO, IT'S NOT WORKING.

991
00:35:17,181 --> 00:35:19,884
Yaya: THIS PHOTO SHOOT WAS
SUCH AN EXPERIMENT FOR ME.

992
00:35:20,184 --> 00:35:22,453
I WENT INTO IT
THINKING,

993
00:35:22,687 --> 00:35:24,822
"DON'T DO ANYTHING DANCE-Y
AT ALL,"

994
00:35:25,156 --> 00:35:27,091
AND I WAS MAD
AT MYSELF FOR A MOMENT.

995
00:35:27,558 --> 00:35:28,926
Tyra: AND YOU SHOULD HAVE
BEEN MAD AT YOURSELF.

996
00:35:29,060 --> 00:35:30,628
YOURS WERE THE WORST
OUT OF THE LOT.

997
00:35:31,062 --> 00:35:32,597
THERE'S AN ART
TO TAKING ADVICE.

998
00:35:33,197 --> 00:35:35,166
WHEN SOMEONE TELLS YOU,
"DON'T LOOK LIKE A DANCER,"

999
00:35:35,533 --> 00:35:39,036
IT MEANS LESS CIRQUE DU SOLEIL,
MORE COUTURE, YOU UNDERSTAND?

1000
00:35:39,036 --> 00:35:41,706
SO WHAT YOU DID IS YOU THREW
EVERYTHING OUT THE WINDOW.

1001
00:35:42,006 --> 00:35:44,075
Nigel: YOU WANNA TAKE
YOUR STRENGTH AS AN ATHLETE

1002
00:35:44,075 --> 00:35:45,543
OR YOUR STRENGTH
AS A DANCER

1003
00:35:45,777 --> 00:35:48,246
AND YOUR ELOQUENCE AND THEN
TRANSLATE INTO FASHION.

1004
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:50,648
Yaya: IT'S--IT'S HARD
FINDING THAT BALANCE, YOU KNOW?

1005
00:35:51,115 --> 00:35:52,049
YEAH. UM...

1006
00:35:54,585 --> 00:35:55,987
Janice: I'D LIKE TO SEE THAT
IN THE PICTURES.

1007
00:35:56,587 --> 00:35:57,054
THAT WAS GOOD.

1008
00:35:58,022 --> 00:35:59,457
Yaya: BUT, UM,
YEAH, IT'S DEEP.

1009
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:00,358
I'M GONNA FIND
THE BALANCE.

1010
00:36:01,025 --> 00:36:01,793
Tyra: WHAT DO YOU THINK
ABOUT THAT PICTURE?

1011
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:03,194
Yaya: OH,
I DON'T LIKE IT.

1012
00:36:03,594 --> 00:36:04,195
Tyra: I DON'T
LIKE IT EITHER.

1013
00:36:04,195 --> 00:36:04,829
YAYA, THANKS.

1014
00:36:05,196 --> 00:36:05,763
Yaya: THANK YOU.

1015
00:36:06,664 --> 00:36:07,665
Tyra: LAST,
WE HAVE ANN.

1016
00:36:08,299 --> 00:36:09,200
YOU HAD
A PHOTO SHOOT

1017
00:36:09,634 --> 00:36:11,035
WHERE YOU HAD TO HIKE
14 FLIGHTS OF STAIRS,

1018
00:36:11,636 --> 00:36:12,703
AND HERE ARE
YOUR THREE SHOTS.

1019
00:36:13,704 --> 00:36:14,605
SOMEBODY'S TIRED.

1020
00:36:15,540 --> 00:36:16,574
Janice: AH,
IT'S PEDESTRIAN.

1021
00:36:17,241 --> 00:36:18,810
Tyra: YOUR MOUTH
IS A LITTLE OPEN.

1022
00:36:18,810 --> 00:36:20,278
Nolé: JUST DON'T KNOW
WHO YOU ARE AS A MODEL.

1023
00:36:20,278 --> 00:36:21,779
YOU'RE NOT
GETTING IT.

1024
00:36:22,113 --> 00:36:23,581
Tyra: HERE IS
YOUR BEST SHOT.

1025
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:25,750
Nolé: OKAY,
THAT SCARES ME, TOO.

1026
00:36:26,551 --> 00:36:27,318
Nigel: I DON'T LIKE
THIS VERY MUCH.

1027
00:36:27,819 --> 00:36:30,188
Nolé: ANN, I MEAN,
YOU'RE SO GORGEOUS,

1028
00:36:30,822 --> 00:36:32,223
BUT IT'S NOT COMING ACROSS
IN THESE PHOTOS AT ALL.

1029
00:36:32,757 --> 00:36:34,192
Janice: YOU WERE
WORKING HERE,

1030
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:35,393
PHOTOGRAPH
IS NOT WORKING,

1031
00:36:35,793 --> 00:36:37,995
AND THERE'S NO "IFs," "ANDs"
OR "BUTs" ABOUT IT.

1032
00:36:37,995 --> 00:36:39,030
IT SUCKS. SORRY.

1033
00:36:44,035 --> 00:36:44,702
Tyra: YAYA.

1034
00:36:45,636 --> 00:36:46,604
Janice: I HOPE
SHE DOESN'T LOSE

1035
00:36:46,604 --> 00:36:47,338
HER DANCE TRAINING
TOO MUCH.

1036
00:36:47,772 --> 00:36:49,006
Nigel: IT'S ABOUT
MODERATION,

1037
00:36:49,006 --> 00:36:50,875
KNOW WHEN TO TURN IT ON,
WHEN IT TURN IT OFF.

1038
00:36:51,175 --> 00:36:51,843
Tyra: AMANDA.

1039
00:36:52,577 --> 00:36:53,811
GOING THROUGH THE FILM,
I WAS LIKE, "WHOA!"

1040
00:36:54,145 --> 00:36:55,913
THIS LOOKS LIKE THE PICTURES
OF GIRLS THAT I WORK WITH.

1041
00:36:55,913 --> 00:36:57,114
NICOLE.

1042
00:36:57,615 --> 00:36:59,951
Nolé: I HAVE NOT BEEN
A BIG FAN OF NICOLE AT ALL,

1043
00:37:00,618 --> 00:37:02,253
BUT IN THIS IMAGE,
SHE SLAMS IT.

1044
00:37:02,653 --> 00:37:04,121
Janice: NEVER GIVE UP
ON TOP MODEL.

1045
00:37:04,121 --> 00:37:04,922
Tyra: NORELLE.

1046
00:37:04,922 --> 00:37:07,258
Nigel: NORELLE REALLY DID
A GOOD JOB IN THIS PICTURE.

1047
00:37:07,258 --> 00:37:08,359
Janice: NORELLE IS IN.

1048
00:37:08,359 --> 00:37:09,327
Tyra: TOCCARA.

1049
00:37:09,861 --> 00:37:10,461
Nolé: I'M ALWAYS GONNA BE
ON HER SIDE.

1050
00:37:10,995 --> 00:37:11,863
Janice: 'CAUSE YOU'RE
A PLUS-SIZED GIRL, HONEY.

1051
00:37:11,863 --> 00:37:13,564
Nolé: THAT'S RIGHT, HONEY,
AND PROUD OF IT.

1052
00:37:13,798 --> 00:37:16,567
Nigel: TOCCARA PHOTOGRAPHS
INCREDIBLY WELL NORMALLY.

1053
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:18,903
THIS IS JUST NOT
HER GENRE.

1054
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:20,004
Tyra: EVA.

1055
00:37:20,638 --> 00:37:22,273
Nolé: I ABSOLUTELY
ADORE EVA.

1056
00:37:22,707 --> 00:37:23,741
Nigel: I THINK SHE HAS
A LOT GOING FOR HER.

1057
00:37:23,875 --> 00:37:24,308
Kate: EVA'S IN.

1058
00:37:24,442 --> 00:37:25,009
Tyra: ANN.

1059
00:37:25,076 --> 00:37:26,410
Kate: I DON'T THINK
ANN IS PHOTOGENIC,

1060
00:37:26,844 --> 00:37:28,746
AND IT'S SUCH
A DISAPPOINTMENT.

1061
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:30,548
Tyra: I THINK
ANN IS PHOTOGENIC.

1062
00:37:30,548 --> 00:37:32,183
SHE JUST DOESN'T KNOW
WHAT THE HELL TO DO

1063
00:37:32,183 --> 00:37:34,452
WITH HER FACE
OR HER BODY.

1064
00:37:34,619 --> 00:37:36,487
I FEEL LIKE HER AND KELLE
ARE NECK AND NECK--

1065
00:37:36,487 --> 00:37:38,522
PRETTY GIRLS,
DON'T KNOW HOW TO MODEL.

1066
00:37:38,823 --> 00:37:39,657
KELLE.

1067
00:37:39,657 --> 00:37:40,758
Nigel: WHATEVER SHE DOES,
SHE OVERTHINKS IT

1068
00:37:40,758 --> 00:37:43,160
AND SORT
OF SCREWS IT UP.

1069
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:43,494
Kate: I THINK
SHE SEES IT

1070
00:37:43,494 --> 00:37:44,762
LIKE THE WAY I CAN LOOK
AT PICASSO

1071
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:47,298
AND SAY, "THAT'S
A GREAT PIECE OF ARTWORK,"

1072
00:37:47,298 --> 00:37:48,933
BUT I DON'T KNOW
HOW TO DO THAT.

1073
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:50,534
Nigel: I THINK SHE DOES HAVE
A PRETTY FACE,

1074
00:37:50,534 --> 00:37:52,236
AND SHE'S
CERTAINLY LOVELY IN PERSON.

1075
00:37:52,236 --> 00:37:53,437
Janice: I THINK SHE SHOULD
GO BACK TO HER ART GALLERY

1076
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:55,773
AND SELL ART
FOR THE REST OF HER LIFE.

1077
00:37:56,073 --> 00:37:56,440
Tyra: CASSIE.

1078
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:59,610
Janice: CASSIE DOESN'T HAVE
A CLUE OF WHAT A MODEL IS ABOUT,

1079
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:01,646
AND THIS PHOTOGRAPH
PROVES IT.

1080
00:38:01,646 --> 00:38:04,115
Nigel: HER FACE LOOKS
SORT OF ALMOST DEAD.

1081
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:05,182
I'M VERY SURPRISED.

1082
00:38:05,182 --> 00:38:06,684
SHE'S A REALLY
PRETTY, PRETTY GIRL.

1083
00:38:06,684 --> 00:38:08,953
Kate: IF CASSIE HAD
MORE LIFE BEHIND HER EYES,

1084
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:11,322
I MIGHT SEE MORE
OF HER BEAUTY.

1085
00:38:11,322 --> 00:38:13,257
Janice: SHE'S
JUST BLECCH.

1086
00:38:21,365 --> 00:38:23,334
Tyra: NINE BEAUTIFUL LADIES
STAND BEFORE ME,

1087
00:38:23,334 --> 00:38:27,705
BUT I ONLY HAVE EIGHT PHOTOS
IN MY HANDS,

1088
00:38:28,172 --> 00:38:31,208
AND THESE PHOTOS REPRESENT
THE EIGHT OF YOU THAT WILL

1089
00:38:31,208 --> 00:38:33,044
STILL BE IN THE RUNNING
TOWARDS BECOMING

1090
00:38:33,044 --> 00:38:34,879
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

1091
00:38:36,681 --> 00:38:37,748
EVA.

1092
00:38:39,583 --> 00:38:43,220
THIS PICTURE IS
ABSOLUTELY BEAUTIFUL.

1093
00:38:43,454 --> 00:38:44,956
CONGRATULATIONS.

1094
00:38:44,956 --> 00:38:46,123
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING
TOWARDS BECOMING

1095
00:38:46,123 --> 00:38:47,258
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

1096
00:38:47,258 --> 00:38:48,159
Eva: THANK YOU.

1097
00:38:48,259 --> 00:38:49,060
Tyra: YOU'RE WELCOME.

1098
00:38:51,996 --> 00:38:52,964
AMANDA.

1099
00:38:54,265 --> 00:38:55,232
NICOLE.

1100
00:38:56,267 --> 00:38:56,968
CONGRATULATIONS.

1101
00:38:57,702 --> 00:38:58,903
YAYA.

1102
00:39:02,340 --> 00:39:04,575
YAYA, YOU KNOW EXACTLY
WHAT I'M GONNA SAY TO YOU.

1103
00:39:05,409 --> 00:39:08,612
IT'S ALL ABOUT BALANCE
AND TAKING CRITIQUE

1104
00:39:08,612 --> 00:39:10,881
AND TAKING IT ALL IN

1105
00:39:11,115 --> 00:39:12,383
AND THEN DOING
THE SUM OF THAT

1106
00:39:12,383 --> 00:39:14,719
AND COMING UP WITH WHAT
WORKS FOR YOU.

1107
00:39:14,719 --> 00:39:16,253
CONGRATULATIONS.

1108
00:39:16,253 --> 00:39:17,421
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING
TOWARDS BECOMING

1109
00:39:17,421 --> 00:39:18,622
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

1110
00:39:18,622 --> 00:39:19,757
Yaya: THANK YOU.

1111
00:39:22,093 --> 00:39:23,227
Tyra: TOCCARA.

1112
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:25,863
NORELLE.

1113
00:39:27,031 --> 00:39:28,299
CONGRATULATIONS.

1114
00:39:28,666 --> 00:39:29,967
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING
TOWARDS BECOMING

1115
00:39:29,967 --> 00:39:31,202
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

1116
00:39:31,502 --> 00:39:32,336
YOU'RE WELCOME.

1117
00:39:37,675 --> 00:39:39,744
Tyra: THE NEXT NAME
THAT I'M GOING TO CALL...

1118
00:39:42,947 --> 00:39:43,914
IS CASSIE.

1119
00:39:46,083 --> 00:39:47,351
CASSIE,
YOU LOOK AMAZING.

1120
00:39:47,351 --> 00:39:49,720
YOU LOOK LIKE
A REAL MODEL.

1121
00:39:50,054 --> 00:39:52,256
I NOTICE A CERTAIN SADNESS
WITH YOU.

1122
00:39:52,256 --> 00:39:53,190
I THINK MAYBE TALKING
TO SOMEONE,

1123
00:39:53,190 --> 00:39:54,959
YOU COULD KINDA
GET THAT OUT.

1124
00:39:55,192 --> 00:39:56,293
CONGRATULATIONS.

1125
00:39:56,293 --> 00:39:57,328
Cassie: THANK YOU.

1126
00:39:57,328 --> 00:39:57,728
Tyra: YOU'RE WELCOME.

1127
00:39:58,529 --> 00:40:00,398
WILL ANN AND KELLE
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

1128
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:07,104
Tyra: I ONLY HAVE
ONE PHOTO IN MY HANDS,

1129
00:40:07,538 --> 00:40:09,073
AND THIS PHOTO REPRESENTS
THE GIRL

1130
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:11,609
THAT WILL CONTINUE ON
IN THE RUNNING TOWARDS BECOMING

1131
00:40:11,609 --> 00:40:13,310
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

1132
00:40:14,111 --> 00:40:16,881
I WILL ONLY
CALL ONE NAME.

1133
00:40:17,014 --> 00:40:18,549
THE GIRL'S NAME
I DO NOT CALL

1134
00:40:18,549 --> 00:40:21,585
MUST IMMEDIATELY
RETURN TO YOUR APARTMENT,

1135
00:40:22,019 --> 00:40:24,321
PACK YOUR BELONGINGS
AND LEAVE.

1136
00:40:25,456 --> 00:40:27,425
I'VE NEVER HAD
TO DO THIS BEFORE,

1137
00:40:27,558 --> 00:40:32,096
BUT I'M GIVING BOTH OF YOU
THE EXACT SAME CRITIQUE.

1138
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:39,570
BOTH OF YOU, ABSOLUTELY
BEAUTIFUL GIRLS TO THE EYE.

1139
00:40:39,570 --> 00:40:43,340
BUT IT DOESN'T TRANSLATE
TO YOUR PHOTOGRAPHS.

1140
00:40:43,507 --> 00:40:48,512
YOU ALL ARE
THE WALKING SIGNPOST FOR

1141
00:40:48,512 --> 00:40:51,849
"PRETTY GIRL,
NOT PHOTOGENIC,"

1142
00:40:52,316 --> 00:40:57,188
BUT THE JUDGES FEEL
THAT ONE OF YOU MAY HAVE

1143
00:40:57,455 --> 00:41:00,658
A LITTLE BIT MORE POTENTIAL
THAN THE OTHER.

1144
00:41:06,797 --> 00:41:08,265
Tyra: CONGRATULATIONS,
ANN.

1145
00:41:10,101 --> 00:41:11,402
YOU ARE STILL IN THE RUNNING
TOWARDS BECOMING

1146
00:41:11,402 --> 00:41:13,104
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

1147
00:41:13,104 --> 00:41:14,205
Ann: THANK YOU.

1148
00:41:14,205 --> 00:41:15,206
Tyra: THANKS, KELLE.

1149
00:41:15,206 --> 00:41:16,140
Kelle: THANK YOU.

1150
00:41:17,174 --> 00:41:19,009
Toccara: MISS KELLE,
GIVE ME A HUG.

1151
00:41:19,577 --> 00:41:21,045
Kelle: I WOULD HAVE LIKED
TO KEEP TRYING,

1152
00:41:21,045 --> 00:41:22,446
YET ON THE SAME HAND,

1153
00:41:22,446 --> 00:41:24,281
THERE'S ONLY SO MUCH
HUMILIATION I CAN TAKE.

1154
00:41:24,982 --> 00:41:26,383
MAYBE I'M NOT GOOD
AT THIS,

1155
00:41:26,383 --> 00:41:28,119
AND THIS IS WHAT
I'M SUPPOSED TO DO.

1156
00:41:28,452 --> 00:41:30,254
YOU KNOW, NOT EVERYONE'S MEANT
TO MODEL.

1157
00:41:30,254 --> 00:41:31,455
I'VE HIT
ROCK BOTTOM,

1158
00:41:31,455 --> 00:41:34,492
AND I'VE BEEN CALLED
SOME REALLY BAD THINGS,

1159
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:35,693
AND I'VE GROWN
FROM IT.

1160
00:41:35,693 --> 00:41:37,394
YOU KNOW,
I GUESS THEY SAY,

1161
00:41:37,394 --> 00:41:38,729
LIKE, WHAT DOESN'T KILL YOU
MAKES YOU STRONGER.

1162
00:41:49,979 --> 00:41:52,014
Tyra: STAY TUNED FOR SCENES
FROM OUR NEXT EPISODE.

1163
00:41:56,352 --> 00:41:59,689
Tyra: HERE'S WHAT'S COMING UP
ON "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"--

1164
00:41:59,689 --> 00:42:01,390
THE GIRLS GET
THEIR PARTY ON.

1165
00:42:01,390 --> 00:42:03,192
Amanda: WE ALL JUMP
IN THE HOT TUB.

1166
00:42:03,192 --> 00:42:06,095
IT JUST BRINGS OUT
YOUR BAD SIDE.

1167
00:42:06,095 --> 00:42:08,064
Diane: JUST WEAR THE DRESS
AND LOOK BEAUTIFUL.

1168
00:42:08,064 --> 00:42:09,465
Tyra: FROM
DIANE VON FURSTENBERG

1169
00:42:09,465 --> 00:42:11,067
TO CYNTHIA ROWLEY,

1170
00:42:11,067 --> 00:42:13,135
THE GIRLS MEET SOME
OF NEW YORK'S TOP DESIGNERS.

1171
00:42:13,135 --> 00:42:14,871
Woman: DO YOU THINK
THAT I'M GONNA BE ABLE

1172
00:42:14,871 --> 00:42:17,740
TO GET A RACK LIKE THIS
IN YOUR SIZE?

1173
00:42:17,740 --> 00:42:20,743
Tyra: BUT IS HIGH FASHION
READY FOR PLUS-SIZED TOCCARA?

1174
00:42:20,743 --> 00:42:23,012
Toccara:
(screams) MY BACK!

